,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"If you haven’t already, check out our [contributing guidelines](https://github.com/Expensify/ReactNativeChat/blob/main/contributingGuides/CONTRIBUTING.md) for onboarding and email contributors@expensify.com to request to join our Slack channel!\n___\n\n**Version Number:** v9.4.5-1\n**Reproducible in staging?:** Yes\n**Reproducible in production?:** Yes\n**If this was caught during regression testing, add the test name, ID and link from BrowserStack:** N/A\n**Email or phone of affected tester (no customers):** N/A\n**Issue reported by:** Applause Internal Team\n**Bug source:** Exploratory - Significant User Experience Deterioration\n**Device used:** Windows 11/ Chrome\n**App Component:** Other\n\n## Action Performed:\n1. Sign in to staging.new.expensify.com \n2. Create a group with more than 2 members\n3. Navigate to the group created in step 2\n4. Click on group header > Members\n5. Hover over the email address of the group admin\n6. Hover over the email address of the member (Not admin)\n\n## Expected Result:\nTooltip with email address of the member is displayed when hovering just like when hovering over admin\n\n## Actual Result:\nTooltip with email address is not displayed when hovering over group member just like when hovering over group admins\n\n## Workaround:\nUnknown\n\n## Platforms:\n- [ ] Android: App\n- [ ] Android: mWeb Chrome\n- [ ] iOS: App\n- [ ] iOS: mWeb Safari\n- [ ] iOS: mWeb Chrome\n- [x] Windows: Chrome\n- [ ] MacOS: Chrome Safari\n\n## Screenshots/Videos\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/340bec63-0c25-468f-9dc8-7fee832bc21f\n\n[View all open jobs on GitHub](https://github.com/Expensify/App/issues?q=is%3Aopen+is%3Aissue+label%3A%22Help+Wanted%22)\n\n\n> **Applause Internal Information**\n> Exported by: Svetlana Lazutkina\n> Bug ID: 7178138\n<details><summary>Upwork Automation - Do Not Edit</summary>\n    <ul>\n        <li>Upwork Job URL: <a href=\"https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~022065147761627713217\">https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~022065147761627713217</a></li>\n        <li>Upwork Job ID: 2065147761627713217</li>\n        <li>Last Price Increase: 2026-07-02</li>\n    </ul>\n</details>","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/93322/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/93322/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alulaalmi/Apache-APISIX/issues/1","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alulaalmi/Apache-APISIX","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alulaalmi/Apache-APISIX/issues/1/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alulaalmi/Apache-APISIX/issues/1/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alulaalmi/Apache-APISIX/issues/1/events","html_url":"https://github.com/alulaalmi/Apache-APISIX/issues/1","id":4661667359,"node_id":"I_kwDOS641NM8AAAABFdtmHw","number":1,"title":"🎯 Fix Stale Upstream Nodes in Kubernetes EndpointSlice Discovery Provider","user":{"login":"alulaalmi","id":293716045,"node_id":"U_kgDOEYHATQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/293716045?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alulaalmi","html_url":"https://github.com/alulaalmi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alulaalmi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alulaalmi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alulaalmi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alulaalmi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alulaalmi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alulaalmi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alulaalmi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alulaalmi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alulaalmi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11237168463,"node_id":"LA_kwDOS641NM8AAAACncmVTw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alulaalmi/Apache-APISIX/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null},{"id":11237168466,"node_id":"LA_kwDOS641NM8AAAACncmVUg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alulaalmi/Apache-APISIX/labels/opire","name":"opire","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null},{"id":11237168467,"node_id":"LA_kwDOS641NM8AAAACncmVUw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alulaalmi/Apache-APISIX/labels/$10","name":"$10","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":9,"created_at":"2026-06-15T02:55:32Z","updated_at":"2026-07-02T02:25:54Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## 📝 Description\nWhen using the Apache APISIX Kubernetes service discovery module (`discovery: kubernetes`), APISIX can continue routing traffic to deleted or terminating Kubernetes endpoints after an `EndpointSlice` update. \n\nThis issue occurs because the Kubernetes discovery provider in APISIX does not correctly reconcile `MODIFIED` or `DELETED` events for `EndpointSlice` resources, or fails to filter out endpoints where the `conditions.ready` status is `false` (or when the endpoint is completely removed from the `endpoints` array in the `EndpointSlice` object). As a result, stale IP addresses remain in the APISIX upstream node list, leading to intermittent `502 Bad Gateway` or `504 Gateway Timeout` errors during application scale-downs, rolling updates, or pod deletions.\n\n## 🎯 Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] APISIX must correctly parse `EndpointSlice` updates and immediately remove endpoints that are no longer present in the `endpoints` list.\n- [ ] Endpoints with `conditions.ready = false` (or missing/terminating states) must be filtered out and excluded from the active upstream nodes, unless explicitly configured otherwise.\n- [ ] The Kubernetes discovery module must handle `DELETED` events for `EndpointSlice` resources by clearing all associated nodes from the corresponding upstream.\n- [ ] Ensure that configuration updates triggered by `EndpointSlice` changes do not cause memory leaks or CPU spikes in the Nginx worker processes.\n- [ ] Add unit/integration tests verifying that scaling down a Kubernetes deployment correctly updates the APISIX upstream nodes in real-time.\n\n## 🛠️ Technical Specifications & Context\nThe Kubernetes service discovery logic is implemented in Lua within the APISIX core. \n\n### Key Files:\n- `/apisix/discovery/kubernetes/init.lua`: Contains the core initialization and registry logic for the Kubernetes discovery provider.\n- `/apisix/discovery/kubernetes/informer.lua` (or equivalent watch/informer implementation): Handles the HTTP long-polling/watch connection to the Kubernetes API server for `endpointslices` resources.\n- `/apisix/discovery/kubernetes/client.lua`: Manages the API queries and deserialization of Kubernetes resources.\n\n### Implementation Details:\n1. **EndpointSlice Structure**: In Kubernetes, an `EndpointSlice` contains an `endpoints` array. Each endpoint has an `addresses` array and a `conditions` map:\n   ```json\n   {\n     \"addresses\": [\"10.244.0.15\"],\n     \"conditions\": {\n       \"ready\": false,\n       \"serving\": false,\n       \"terminating\": true\n     }\n   }\n   ```\n2. **Filtering Logic**: In `/apisix/discovery/kubernetes/init.lua`, ensure the parser checks `conditions.ready`. If `ready` is not `true`, the address must be excluded from the upstream node list.\n3. **Event Handling**: Ensure that when a `MODIFIED` event is received for an `EndpointSlice`, the local cache is fully synchronized (diffed or overwritten) with the new list of active endpoints, rather than appending or failing to prune stale entries.\n\n## 🧪 Verification & Testing\n\n### Manual Verification Steps:\n1. Deploy a local Kubernetes cluster (e.g., Minikube or Kind).\n2. Configure APISIX with the Kubernetes discovery provider enabled in `config.yaml`:\n   ```yaml\n   discovery:\n     kubernetes:\n       service:\n         schema: https\n         host: ${KUBERNETES_SERVICE_HOST}\n         port: ${KUBERNETES_SERVICE_PORT}\n   ```\n3. Create a test deployment with 3 replicas and expose it via a Kubernetes Service.\n4. Configure an APISIX Route pointing to the service using the discovery mechanism:\n   ```json\n   {\n     \"uri\": \"/test\",\n     \"upstream\": {\n       \"type\": \"roundrobin\",\n       \"discovery_type\": \"kubernetes\",\n       \"service_name\": \"default/test-service\"\n     }\n   }\n   ```\n5. Scale the deployment down to 1 replica:\n   ```bash\n   kubectl scale deployment test-deployment --replicas=1\n   ```\n6. Query the APISIX Control Plane / Control API (e.g., `/v1/discovery/kubernetes/show`) or monitor the APISIX error logs to verify that the upstream node list immediately shrinks to 1 IP address and no traffic is routed to the 2 deleted pod IPs.\n\n### Automated Tests:\n- Add a test case in `t/discovery/kubernetes.t` (using the `Test::Nginx` framework) that mocks `EndpointSlice` updates (specifically transitions from `ready: true` to `ready: false` and endpoint deletions) and asserts the upstream registry state.\n\n---\n\n[![Opire Bounty](https://img.shields.io/badge/bounty-Opire-emerald?style=for-the-badge)](https://github.com/alulaalmi/Apache-APISIX)\n<br/>\n<hr/>\n\n<details><summary>This repo is using Opire - what does it mean? 👇</summary><br/>💵 Everyone can add rewards for this issue commenting <code>/reward 100</code> (replace <code>100</code> with the amount).<br/>🕵️‍♂️ If someone starts working on this issue to earn the rewards, they can comment <code>/try</code> to let everyone know!<br/>🙌 And when they open the PR, they can comment <code>/claim #1</code> either in the PR description or in a PR's comment.<br/><br/>🪙 Also, everyone can tip any user commenting <code>/tip 20 @alulaalmi</code> (replace <code>20</code> with the amount, and <code>@alulaalmi</code> with the user to tip).<br/><br/>📖 If you want to learn more, check out our <a href=\"https://docs.opire.dev\">documentation</a>.</details>","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alulaalmi/Apache-APISIX/issues/1/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alulaalmi/Apache-APISIX/issues/1/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramimbo/mergework/issues/933","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramimbo/mergework","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramimbo/mergework/issues/933/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramimbo/mergework/issues/933/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramimbo/mergework/issues/933/events","html_url":"https://github.com/ramimbo/mergework/issues/933","id":4595825805,"node_id":"I_kwDOSlxd2c8AAAABEe68jQ","number":933,"title":"MRWK bounty: 40 MRWK - review open MergeWork PRs with evidence, round 20","user":{"login":"ramimbo","id":160272258,"node_id":"U_kgDOCY2Pgg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/160272258?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramimbo","html_url":"https://github.com/ramimbo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramimbo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramimbo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramimbo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramimbo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramimbo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramimbo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramimbo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramimbo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramimbo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11032959473,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSlxd2c8AAAACkZ2Z8Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramimbo/mergework/labels/mrwk:bounty","name":"mrwk:bounty","color":"0E7C66","default":false,"description":"MRWK bounty is posted"},{"id":11034379803,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSlxd2c8AAAACkbNGGw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramimbo/mergework/labels/review","name":"review","color":"5319E7","default":false,"description":"Code review and PR review work"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":167,"created_at":"2026-06-05T09:26:37Z","updated_at":"2026-07-01T07:18:07Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"<!-- mergework:mrwk:live-bounty-status:start -->\n**MergeWork status:** live bounty\n\nReserved on MergeWork: https://mrwk.online/bounties/114\n\nClaims are open only while the public bounty row remains open and effective award capacity remains. Use the public bounty page or API as the authoritative current status.\n<!-- mergework:mrwk:live-bounty-status:end -->\n\n## MRWK Bounty\n\nReward: `40 MRWK per accepted award`\nMax awards: `30`\n\n## Work Needed\n\nReview open MergeWork pull requests with concrete current-head evidence. This round is proposed early so review capacity is ready before the current review rounds empty.\n\n## Priority Targets\n\n- Clean, mergeable contributor PRs that are close to acceptance.\n- PRs that affect treasury, bounty lifecycle, admin flow, deployment, documentation, MCP behavior, public bounty discovery, or queue safety.\n- Blocker reviews on stale-looking, dirty, or workflow-gated PRs where the review gives maintainers a clear close, fix, approve-workflow, or rebase decision.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\nAccepted reviews must:\n\n- be by someone other than the PR author;\n- link a GitHub PR review or concise PR comment;\n- review the current head, or clearly state the reviewed head SHA;\n- include concrete evidence such as files inspected, behavior checked, commands run, CI reviewed, mergeability checked, duplicate or overlap checked, or a specific actionable finding;\n- avoid treating proposed, pending, closed, exhausted, or unsupported bounty references as claimable.\n\n## How To Submit\n\nComment here with the PR review URL or PR comment URL and include `Bounty #<this issue number>` or `Refs #<this issue number>`.\n\n## Evidence or Tests Required\n\nUse a short review packet:\n\n- Reviewed PR:\n- Head commit:\n- Files inspected:\n- Verdict:\n- Validation:\n\n## Out of Scope\n\n- Rubber-stamp approvals, vague comments, self-reviews, stale-head reviews that do not account for current code, or duplicate reviews that add no new evidence.\n- Reviews that call bad work merge-ready while missing a central behavior problem.\n- Reviews containing private secrets, private vulnerability details, fabricated payout claims, price claims, investment claims, exchange/liquidity claims, or bridge/cash-out claims.\n\n## Duplicate and Stale Work Rules\n\nDuplicate work is judged by the first useful, evidence-backed review for the same PR head and core finding. Stale reviews may be skipped if the PR head changes materially before acceptance. Reviews may identify blockers and still qualify if they give maintainers concrete action.","