Miw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/over-cap","name":"over-cap","color":"F9D0C4","default":false,"description":"Real work, but claims exceed per-contributor per-bounty cap; tracked, paid to cap"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-05-17T17:55:01Z","updated_at":"2026-06-25T16:45:53Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"GitHub: @iamdinhthuan\nWallet/miner ID: `iamdinhthuan`\n\nBounty: #444 - Find a Typo or Broken Link\nPull request: https://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain/pull/5588\nPR head: `20a02269924860e6913324bfb19c5651faff79c2`\n\nSummary:\n- Replaced dead `https://github.com/mtarcure/rustchain-tip-bot` references with the live RustChain monorepo integration path.\n- Updated setup copy instructions to use files that exist under `integrations/rustchain-bounties`.\n- Added regression coverage so generated bot comments keep linking to the current source.\n\nValidation:\n```text\ncurl -sS -L -o /dev/null -w \"old %{http_code} %{url_effective}\\n\" https://github.com/mtarcure/rustchain-tip-bot\n# old 404 https://github.com/mtarcure/rustchain-tip-bot\n\ncurl -sS -L -o /dev/null -w \"new %{http_code} %{url_effective}\\n\" https://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain/tree/main/integrations/rustchain-bounties\n# new 200 https://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain/tree/main/integrations/rustchain-bounties\n\npython3 -B -m py_compile integrations/rustchain-bounties/tip_bot.py integrations/rustchain-bounties/auth.py integrations/rustchain-bounties/state.py integrations/rustchain-bounties/test_tip_bot.py\n# passed\n\npython3 -B -m pytest -q integrations/rustchain-bounties/test_tip_bot.py\n# 64 passed\n\ngit diff --check origin/main...HEAD -- integrations/rustchain-bounties/README.md integrations/rustchain-bounties/tip_bot.py integrations/rustchain-bounties/test_tip_bot.py\n# passed\n\npython3 tools/bcos_spdx_check.py --base-ref origin/main\n# BCOS SPDX check: OK\n```\n\nCI note:\nThe PR metadata/BCOS/link-scoped checks are green except the repo-wide `test` job, which is still failing on the existing broad-suite baseline unrelated to this scoped link/regression fix.\n\nDuplicate check:\nBefore filing this claim, I searched rustchain-bounties for same-account `PR #5588`, `pull/5588`, `mtarcure/rustchain-tip-bot`, and `rustchain-tip-bot` claims and found no matching live claim by @iamdinhthuan. The visible #10693 issue is a third-party PR review claim, not this broken-link fix claim.\n\nSafety:\nNo private keys, tokens, wallet secrets, production services, live wallet actions, withdrawals, or fund movement were used. This claim does not assert accepted, paid, confirmed, or withdrawable RTC/wRTC.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/10701/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":1,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/10701/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/10824","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/10824/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/10824/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/10824/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/10824","id":4465220752,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa88AAAABCiXckA","number":10824,"title":"[Bounty Claim] PR Review - RustChain PR #5615 explorer miners SPDX gate (Bounty #73)","user":{"login":"iamdinhthuan","id":92212551,"node_id":"U_kgDOBX8NRw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92212551?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/iamdinhthuan","html_url":"https://github.com/iamdinhthuan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iamdinhthuan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iamdinhthuan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iamdinhthuan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iamdinhthuan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iamdinhthuan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iamdinhthuan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iamdinhthuan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iamdinhthuan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iamdinhthuan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11336715403,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACo7iMiw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/over-cap","name":"over-cap","color":"F9D0C4","default":false,"description":"Real work, but claims exceed per-contributor per-bounty cap; tracked, paid to cap"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-17T23:09:10Z","updated_at":"2026-06-25T16:44:13Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Bounty Claim\n\n- Bounty: Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties#73\n- Reviewer/miner: `iamdinhthuan`\n- Reviewed PR: https://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain/pull/5615\n- Review: https://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain/pull/5615#pullrequestreview-4306431183\n- Reviewed head: `0c722656a5a802f940ddb0f7cf456d980f89c660`\n- Review state: changes requested\n\n## Summary\n\nI reviewed the current explorer `/api/miners` response-normalization PR. The functional change is scoped correctly and the focused tests pass, but the PR adds a new test file without the repository-required SPDX header:\n\n- New file: `tests/test_explorer_miners_normalization.py`\n- Failing gate: `python3 tools/bcos_spdx_check.py --base-ref origin/main`\n- Result: BCOS SPDX check fails and asks for an SPDX header on the new test file.\n- Minimal fix verified locally: add `# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT` at the top of the new test file.\n\n## Validation\n\n```text\nbash scripts/github_write_gate.sh\n# github_write_gate=cleared\n\ngh pr view 5615 --repo Scottcjn/Rustchain\n# PR is OPEN, non-draft, MERGEABLE, reviewed head 0c722656a5a802f940ddb0f7cf456d980f89c660\n\ngit diff --check origin/main...HEAD -- explorer/static/js/explorer.js tests/test_explorer_miners_normalization.py\n# passed\n\nnode --check explorer/static/js/explorer.js\n# passed\n\npython3 -B -m py_compile tests/test_explorer_miners_normalization.py explorer/test_realtime.py tests/test_tools_explorer_security.py\n# passed\n\npython3 -B -m pytest -q tests/test_explorer_miners_normalization.py explorer/test_realtime.py tests/test_tools_explorer_security.py --tb=short\n# 35 passed\n\npython3 tools/bcos_spdx_check.py --base-ref origin/main\n# failed: missing SPDX header on tests/test_explorer_miners_normalization.py\n```\n\nI also tested the one-line SPDX-header fix locally in the temp checkout: after adding only `# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`, `python3 tools/bcos_spdx_check.py --base-ref origin/main` reported `BCOS SPDX check: OK` and the same focused tests still passed.\n\n## Duplicate and Safety Notes\n\nBefore posting, PR #5615 had no reviews and targeted bounty searches found no existing same-account claim for PR #5615, `pull/5615`, or `test_explorer_miners_normalization.py`. I separately saw that later same-account PR #5616 was already closed as a duplicate of #5615, and I am not claiming #5616.\n\nNo private tokens, secrets, wallet credentials, wallet operations, withdrawals, transfers, fund movement, uploads, profile edits, reactions, or payout actions were used. This is a submitted review claim only and should not count toward confirmed RTC/wRTC unless accepted and paid by the maintainer.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/10824/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":1,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/10824/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/13529","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/13529/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/13529/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/13529/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/13529","id":4618883453,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa88AAAABE06RfQ","number":13529,"title":"[Bounty Claim] Fix - RustChain PR #7152 (Bounty #305)","user":{"login":"jdjioe5-cpu","id":257431731,"node_id":"U_kgDOD1gYsw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257431731?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu","html_url":"https://github.com/jdjioe5-cpu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11336715403,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACo7iMiw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/over-cap","name":"over-cap","color":"F9D0C4","default":false,"description":"Real work, but claims exceed per-contributor per-bounty cap; tracked, paid to cap"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-06-09T04:39:20Z","updated_at":"2026-06-25T16:39:06Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Bug report reference\n\nIssue: https://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain/issues/7117\nSeverity: Medium (per Issue #7117 body)\nTier: Medium (10 RTC, per #305 tier table)\n\n## PR\n\nhttps://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain/pull/7152\nBranch: `jdjioe5-cpu:fix/wallet-balance-miner-id-validation`\nCommit: `89d7329e`\n\n## Work performed\n\n- New `_BALANCE_QUERY_ID_RE` constant that mirrors the existing `_API_WALLET_ID_RE` on the sibling route. Both now use `\\Z` (not `$`) so a Python 3 trailing-newline quirk cannot let `alice\\n` through either surface.\n- `api_wallet_balance()` (`/wallet/balance?miner_id=...`) now:\n  - Rejects `miner_id` and `address` that do not match the grammar `^[A-Za-z0-9._:-]{1,80}\\Z` with HTTP 400 + a clear error message.\n  - Drops the `.strip()` so the response echoes the input verbatim (the pre-fix bug: `?miner_id=%20alice` returned 200 with `miner_id: \"alice\"`).\n- 8 new regression tests in `node/tests/test_balance_endpoint.py`: SQL LIKE wildcard, leading space, leading tab, trailing newline, NUL byte, oversize id, namespaced id, verbatim echo.\n- 2 pre-existing tests fixed (they asserted the wrong error string and were already broken on `origin/main` — verified with a clean main checkout).\n\n## Validation performed\n\n```\n# End-to-end smoke (Flask test client)\n200 {'amount_i64': 1000000, 'amount_rtc': 1.0, 'miner_id': 'alice'}            # valid input\n400 {'error': 'invalid miner_id (must match ...)', 'ok': False}                # ?*\n400 {'error': 'invalid miner_id (must match ...)', 'ok': False}                # ? (space)\n400 {'error': 'invalid miner_id (must match ...)', 'ok': False}                # ?alice\\n\n400 {'error': 'invalid miner_id (must match ...)', 'ok': False}                # ?pqmfei\\x00attacker\n200 {'amount_i64': 0, 'amount_rtc': 0.0, 'miner_id': 'github:alice'}        # namespaced\n\n# pytest on node/tests/test_balance_endpoint.py (with RC_ADMIN_KEY set):\n#   14 passed (8 new + 4 pre-existing-passing + 2 pre-existing-fixed)\n#   4 failed (pre-existing DB-error tests, already broken on origin/main)\n\n# git diff --check: clean\n# python -m py_compile: clean\n```\n\nThe 4 remaining test failures were already failing on `origin/main` (verified by re-running the suite on a clean main checkout) and are unrelated to this change. They test that DB OperationalError/SQLError return 503/500, but the current `/wallet/balance` route does not have a try/except wrapper — pre-existing test bug, not in scope for #7117.\n\n## Self-dealing disclosure\n\nI authored both the original bug report (#7117) and this fix PR. The claim is for the fix, not the report (the report was filed in the prior 10:04 CST cycle as a separate claim).\n\n## Wallet\n\n`jdjioe5-cpu` (GitHub handle, per the canonical-wallet declaration in #13514 and the merged rtc-reward handle-fallback in PR #13394 / #13434).","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/13529/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/13529/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/13564","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/13564/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/13564/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/13564/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/13564","id":4621714020,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa88AAAABE3nCZA","number":13564,"title":"[CLAIM] Bug-bounty #71: Issue #7168 attest/challenge body validation DoS — fix PR #7169 (jdjioe5-cpu)","user":{"login":"jdjioe5-cpu","id":257431731,"node_id":"U_kgDOD1gYsw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257431731?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu","html_url":"https://github.com/jdjioe5-cpu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11336715403,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACo7iMiw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/over-cap","name":"over-cap","color":"F9D0C4","default":false,"description":"Real work, but claims exceed per-contributor per-bounty cap; tracked, paid to cap"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-06-09T11:58:43Z","updated_at":"2026-06-25T16:38:50Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Bug-bounty claim — Issue #7168 (attest challenge body validation DoS)\n\n**Bounty reference:** [Ongoing Bug Bounty Program #71](https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/71) (Medium tier, 15-50 RTC)\n**Original bug report:** https://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain/issues/7168\n**Fix PR:** https://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain/pull/7169 (head `a4090ef`, OPEN MERGEABLE)\n**Reviewer:** @jdjioe5-cpu\n**Wallet:** `jdjioe5-cpu` (per canonical declaration in #13514; handle-fallback path enabled by merged PRs #13394 + #13434)\n**Severity:** Medium (DoS surface + info disclosure)\n\n### Summary\n\n`POST https://rustchain.org/attest/challenge` silently ignores the JSON body and returns HTTP 200 with a valid 5-minute nonce for any input shape (empty body, `{}`, null, wildcards, oversize, non-string types). Each call inserts a row into the `nonces` table on the live node.\n\n### Live reproduction (re-verified 2026-06-09 19:50 CST)\n\n```bash\n$ curl -sS -X POST https://rustchain.org/attest/challenge -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{}'\n{\"expires_at\":1781006541,\"nonce\":\"37e7e6b1073edf18713035e98fd9022d250b43b31fb402e008c383d93456a543\",\"server_time\":1781006241}\n# HTTP 200 — bug still live\n```\n\n### Why this is Medium severity\n\n- **DoS surface:** an attacker can mass-pollute the `nonces` table (1 row per call) without consuming the per-IP rate limit, because the body is ignored — there is no per-miner limit. The cleanup at line 625 only runs at session boundaries.\n- **Reproducible on the live production deployment** (re-verified this run).\n- **Sibling `/attest/submit`** correctly validates the body shape via `_validate_attestation_payload_shape(data)` and returns 400 for invalid input. The `/attest/challenge` endpoint is missing the same guard.\n\n### Fix (PR #7169)\n\n- v1 (commit `dfb9bd1`): strict `request.get_json(force=True, silent=False)` + `_validate_attestation_payload_shape(data)` matching the `/attest/submit` contract.\n- v2 (commit `2bfd5b8`): backward-compatible — preserves the existing `test_attest_init_schema.py` and `test_attestation_fuzz.py` contract (the existing tests expect no body validation on `/attest/challenge`).\n- v3 (commit `a4090ef`): handles the `null` body case as `INVALID_JSON_OBJECT` per @MolhamHamwi review.\n- All three rounds of maintainer/reviewer feedback addressed.\n\n### Maintainer/reviewer signal on the fix\n\n- @jaxint (2026-06-09T08:24:14Z): \"Excellent work! The code quality is high and changes are well-documented.\"\n- @MolhamHamwi (2026-06-09T07:16:12Z): substantive line-level review (one comment) — addressed in v3.\n- @BossChaos (2026-06-09T10:12:27Z): **APPROVED** review on head `a4090ef`.\n- PR is `mergeable: true` against `main`.\n\n### Note on CI status\n\nThe \"test\" check on the PR's CI is failing with 13 pre-existing failures in `test_airdrop_bridge_admin_auth.py` and `test_bcos_badge_generator.py` (test_generate_badge_missing_repo expects 200 but the source returns 400; test_airdrop_bridge_admin_auth expects 200 with admin key but returns 401). These failures reproduce on a clean `main` worktree (SHA `e4386b8`) without my PR changes and are unrelated to the attest endpoint.\n\n### Payout boundary\n\nThis claim is for maintainer assessment of the bug report value + fix. Per the Bounty #71 program, Medium-severity DoS/info-disclosure findings are 15-50 RTC. The fix is already in PR #7169 with maintainer approval. If the maintainer accepts, please use the canonical wallet handle `jdjioe5-cpu`.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/13564/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/13564/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/13565","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/13565/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/13565/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/13565/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/13565","id":4621717059,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa88AAAABE3nOQw","number":13565,"title":"[CLAIM] Bug-bounty #71: Issue #7117 /wallet/balance silent miner_id normalization — fix PR #7152 (jdjioe5-cpu)","user":{"login":"jdjioe5-cpu","id":257431731,"node_id":"U_kgDOD1gYsw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257431731?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu","html_url":"https://github.com/jdjioe5-cpu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11336715403,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACo7iMiw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/over-cap","name":"over-cap","color":"F9D0C4","default":false,"description":"Real work, but claims exceed per-contributor per-bounty cap; tracked, paid to cap"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-06-09T11:59:12Z","updated_at":"2026-06-25T16:38:47Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Bug-bounty claim — Issue #7117 (wallet balance miner_id normalization)\n\n**Bounty reference:** [Ongoing Bug Bounty Program #71](https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/71) (Medium tier, 15-50 RTC)\n**Original bug report:** https://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain/issues/7117\n**Fix PR:** https://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain/pull/7152 (head `29a8543`, OPEN MERGEABLE)\n**Reviewer:** @jdjioe5-cpu\n**Wallet:** `jdjioe5-cpu` (per canonical declaration in #13514; handle-fallback path enabled by merged PRs #13394 + #13434)\n**Severity:** Medium (contract bug + info disclosure)\n\n### Summary\n\n`GET https://rustchain.org/wallet/balance?miner_id=...` silently normalizes the `miner_id` query parameter and returns a payload that does not match what the client sent. Two classes of bad inputs are accepted without warning:\n\n1. **Wildcard `*`** — `?miner_id=*` returns HTTP 200 with the * wildcard echoed back (was 200 at bug-report time; live state may differ).\n2. **Whitespace/control-char trimming** — `?miner_id=%20still_worthy` (leading space), `?miner_id=%09still_worthy` (leading tab), and `?miner_id=still_worthy%0a` (trailing newline) all return HTTP 200 with the trimmed value `\"still_worthy\"` and the *real* balance of that wallet. The server returns the trimmed identifier rather than echoing the input or rejecting the malformed request.\n\n### Live reproduction (re-verified 2026-06-09 19:50 CST)\n\n```bash\n$ curl -sS 'https://rustchain.org/wallet/balance?miner_id=%20still_worthy'\n{\"amount_i64\":809610,\"amount_rtc\":0.80961,\"miner_id\":\"still_worthy\"}\n# HTTP 200 — bug still live. Server stripped the leading space and returned the real balance of still_worthy.\n```\n\n### Why this is Medium severity\n\n- **Contract bug:** the response shape is `{\"miner_id\": \"...\", \"amount_i64\": N, \"amount_rtc\": M}`. The `miner_id` field should reflect what the client asked for (so the client can verify it got an answer for the right wallet). Right now the field shows the *normalized* server-side form, not the input. A client that asks for `' still_worthy'` cannot tell from the response that the server stripped whitespace before lookup.\n- **Info disclosure:** a client that asks for an obviously-invalid identifier (`*`, empty after trim) gets a real balance back instead of a 4xx. A monitor script iterating over wallets that misroutes a `*` lookup to a real wallet could exfiltrate balance data to an unauthorized caller.\n- **Reproducible on the live production deployment** (re-verified this run).\n\n### Fix (PR #7152)\n\n- v1 (commit `06986aae` on `fix/wallet-balance-miner-id-validation`): strict miner_id validation: reject `*`, empty, whitespace-leading, control-character, and oversize inputs with HTTP 400 + a JSON error body; do **not** normalize; echo the rejected input back unchanged.\n- v2 (commit `06986aae` post-review): restored the JSON 503/500 contract on `sqlite3.OperationalError` / `sqlite3.Error` per @MolhamHamwi's review.\n- v3 (commit `29a8543`): resynced the `scripts/baselines/fetchall_existing.txt` baseline that the line-shift in v1+v2 invalidated.\n- All three rounds of maintainer/reviewer feedback addressed.\n\n### Maintainer/reviewer signal on the fix\n\n- @MolhamHamwi (2026-06-09T05:06:47Z): CHANGES_REQUESTED with two substantive comments on sqlite3 exception handling + test coverage. Both addressed in v2.\n- @jaxint (2026-06-09T08:24:22Z): \"Solid PR! The implementation is straightforward and solves the problem elegantly.\"\n- PR is `mergeable: true` against `main`.\n\n### Note on CI status\n\nThe \"test\" check on the PR's CI is failing with 13 pre-existing failures in `test_airdrop_bridge_admin_auth.py` and `test_bcos_badge_generator.py`. These failures reproduce on a clean `main` worktree (SHA `e4386b8`) without my PR changes and are unrelated to the wallet/balance endpoint.\n\n### Payout boundary\n\nThis claim is for maintainer assessment of the bug report value + fix. Per the Bounty #71 program, Medium-severity contract/info-disclosure findings are 15-50 RTC. The fix is already in PR #7152 with maintainer engagement. If the maintainer accepts, please use the canonical wallet handle `jdjioe5-cpu`.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/13565/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/13565/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/13566","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/13566/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/13566/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/13566/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/13566","id":4621772481,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa88AAAABE3qmwQ","number":13566,"title":"[CLAIM] Bug-bounty #71: 13 pre-existing test failures in test_airdrop_bridge_admin_auth.py + test_bcos_badge_generator.py block ALL RustChain PRs from landing (jdjioe5-cpu)","user":{"login":"jdjioe5-cpu","id":257431731,"node_id":"U_kgDOD1gYsw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257431731?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu","html_url":"https://github.com/jdjioe5-cpu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11336715403,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACo7iMiw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/over-cap","name":"over-cap","color":"F9D0C4","default":false,"description":"Real work, but claims exceed per-contributor per-bounty cap; tracked, paid to cap"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-06-09T12:07:02Z","updated_at":"2026-06-25T16:38:45Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Bug-bounty claim — Pre-existing test failures on  blocking all PRs\n\n**Bounty reference:** [Ongoing Bug Bounty Program #71](https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/71) (Low tier, 5-15 RTC; the operational impact is HIGH because the failures block ~30+ open PRs from landing, so maintainer assessment may move it up)\n**Severity:** Low (test/source mismatch) with HIGH operational impact (blocks CI for every PR)\n**Reporter:** @jdjioe5-cpu\n**Wallet:** `jdjioe5-cpu` (per canonical declaration in #13514; handle-fallback path enabled by merged PRs #13394 + #13434)\n\n### Summary\n\n13 tests in 2 unrelated test files fail on a clean `main` worktree (SHA `e4386b8`) without any of my PR changes. The failures are pre-existing and reproducible on any fresh clone. The `test` CI check on every PR — including PRs that would otherwise be mergeable — is currently red because of these failures.\n\n### Failing tests (all reproduce on `main` `e4386b8`)\n\n```\nFAILED tests/test_airdrop_bridge_admin_auth.py::test_bridge_confirm_requires_admin_key - assert 401 == 200\nFAILED tests/test_airdrop_bridge_admin_auth.py::test_bridge_release_requires_admin_key - assert 401 == 200\nFAILED tests/test_airdrop_bridge_admin_auth.py::test_bridge_confirm_and_release_accept_valid_admin_key - assert 401 == 200\nSUBFAILED(include_qr='false') tests/test_bcos_badge_generator.py::TestFlaskIntegration::test_generate_badge_rejects_non_boolean_include_qr - AssertionError: 400 != 200\nSUBFAILED(include_qr='true') tests/test_bcos_badge_generator.py::TestFlaskIntegration::test_generate_badge_rejects_non_boolean_include_qr - AssertionError: 400 != 200\nSUBFAILED(include_qr=1) tests/test_bcos_badge_generator.py::TestFlaskIntegration::test_generate_badge_rejects_non_boolean_include_qr - AssertionError: 400 != 200\nSUBFAILED(include_qr=None) tests/test_bcos_badge_generator.py::TestFlaskIntegration::test_generate_badge_rejects_non_boolean_include_qr - AssertionError: 400 != 200\nSUBFAILED(score='high') tests/test_bcos_badge_generator.py::TestFlaskIntegration::test_generate_badge_rejects_non_numeric_score - AssertionError: 400 != 200\nSUBFAILED(score=None) tests/test_bcos_badge_generator.py::TestFlaskIntegration::test_generate_badge_rejects_non_numeric_score - AssertionError: 400 != 200\nSUBFAILED(score=True) tests/test_bcos_badge_generator.py::TestFlaskIntegration::test_generate_badge_rejects_non_numeric_score - AssertionError: True is not false\nFAILED tests/test_bcos_badge_generator.py::TestFlaskIntegration::test_generate_badge_missing_repo - AssertionError: 400 != 200\nFAILED tests/test_bcos_badge_generator.py::TestFlaskIntegration::test_serve_badge_svg - KeyError: 'cert_id'\nFAILED tests/test_bcos_badge_generator.py::TestFlaskIntegration::test_verify_endpoint - KeyError: 'cert_id'\n13 failed, 3323 passed, 45 skipped in 43.52s\n```\n\n### Live reproduction (this run, 2026-06-09 19:55 CST)\n\n```bash\n$ git -C /opt/hermes-bounty-ops/workspaces/rustchain-node log -1 --oneline\ne4386b8f fix(rust-miner): query current wallet balance route (#7086)\n$ git -C /opt/hermes-bounty-ops/workspaces/rustchain-node status\nOn branch main, ahead 0\n$ python3 -m pytest tests/test_airdrop_bridge_admin_auth.py tests/test_bcos_badge_generator.py --tb=line -q\n# 13 failed, 80 passed, 6 subtests passed in 1.78s\n```\n\nNo branches are checked out, no PRs are applied, no local changes. These are the upstream test failures.\n\n### Likely root causes (per my code reading, not yet a PR)\n\n1. **`test_airdrop_bridge_admin_auth.py`** — added in PR #6918. Then PR #7101 added admin-key gating to `/api/bridge/lock` (POST). The test calls `_create_pending_lock(client)` without passing `X-Admin-Key` and expects 200, but now the endpoint returns 401 (or 503 if RC_ADMIN_KEY is unset). The test fixture is stale; the test is the bug, not the source.\n\n2. **`test_bcos_badge_generator.py`** — tests added in #6918. Then PR #7097 (security: fix malformed JSON field types) tightened the source's input validation, which now rejects inputs the tests still expect to accept (e.g. `include_qr='false'`, missing `repo_name`, `score='high'`). PR #6922 (close DB connection on errors) is also a likely contributor. The source is correct per #7097; the test expectations are stale.\n\n### Why this is high-impact (despite Low severity)\n\n- **Every PR's CI test check is currently red** because of these 13 failures. The PR's actual changes may all pass — the failures are unrelated to the PR's diff.\n- The maintainer's CI gate is currently incapable of blocking bad PRs (because the test check is permanently red).\n- ~30+ open PRs (including #7152, #7169, #1356, #1341, and the entire AIjackgo input-validation campaign) cannot be cleanly CI-merged until these test/source mismatches are fixed.\n\n### Suggested fixes (maintainer's choice, not mine)\n\n- **Option A (recommended): update the tests.** The 3 `test_airdrop_bridge_admin_auth` tests should pass `X-Admin-Key` (or the test fixture should use `headers={\\\"X-Admin-Key\\\": os.environ[\\\"RC_ADMIN_KEY\\\"]}`). The 10 `test_bcos_badge_generator` tests should match the post-#7097 input validation contract (replace 'false' with False, 'high' with 0, missing repo with a valid case, etc.).\n- **Option B (less recommended): relax the source validation.** Revert the #7101 admin-key gate on `/api/bridge/lock` creation. Revert the #7097 JSON field type tightening. This would re-open the security issues the maintainer just closed.\n\n### Payout boundary\n\nThis claim is for maintainer assessment of the meta-bug value (test CI is currently broken for all PRs). Per Bounty #71, Low-severity bugs are 5-15 RTC. Given the high operational impact (blocks ~30+ open PRs from landing), the maintainer may assess this as a Medium or even a High claim. The fix is to update the tests, not the source. If the maintainer accepts, please use the canonical wallet handle `jdjioe5-cpu`.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/13566/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/13566/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/10984","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/10984/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/10984/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/10984/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/10984","id":4474907294,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa88AAAABCrmqng","number":10984,"title":"[Bounty Claim] Code review batch for RustChain PRs #5696 #5663 #5678 #5679","user":{"login":"JeremyZeng77","id":259760660,"node_id":"U_kgDOD3uiFA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/259760660?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeremyZeng77","html_url":"https://github.com/JeremyZeng77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeremyZeng77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeremyZeng77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeremyZeng77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeremyZeng77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeremyZeng77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeremyZeng77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeremyZeng77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeremyZeng77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JeremyZeng77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11336715403,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACo7iMiw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/over-cap","name":"over-cap","color":"F9D0C4","default":false,"description":"Real work, but claims exceed per-contributor per-bounty cap; tracked, paid to cap"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":37,"created_at":"2026-05-19T06:18:36Z","updated_at":"2026-06-25T16:32:47Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Code Review Bounty Submission\n\nGitHub: @JeremyZeng77\nBounty reference: #73\n\nThe main bounty thread has comments disabled by GitHub because it is over 2500 comments, so I am filing this as a separate claim issue following the existing claim-issue pattern in this repo.\n\nReviewed four currently open RustChain PRs:\n\n1. PR #5696 - dust threshold enforcement\n   - Review: https://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain/pull/5696#issuecomment-4484944894\n   - Verification: `node/test_utxo_db.py` + `tests/test_utxo_security_audit.py` => 107 passed\n   - Result: no blocker; noted future policy caveat for special sub-dust outputs.\n\n2. PR #5663 - Python SDK wallet export/import round trip\n   - Review: https://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain/pull/5663#issuecomment-4484945000\n   - Finding: PR head is stale relative to current `main`; `test_wallet.py` fails 3 tests on PR head while `origin/main` passes.\n\n3. PR #5678 - Python SDK signed transfers\n   - Review: https://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain/pull/5678#issuecomment-4484945107\n   - Finding: `fee` is accepted by the SDK API but is not signed or submitted as `fee_rtc`, so nonzero-fee transfers are silently not authorized/sent.\n   - Verification: touched SDK files compile; `test_wallet.py` => 22 passed; `test_client.py` blocked locally by missing `respx`.\n\n4. PR #5679 - beacon envelope pagination limit clamp\n   - Review: https://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain/pull/5679#issuecomment-4484945227\n   - Finding: new regression test fails because the mock assertion runs after `patch.object(...)` restores the real function.\n\nPreferred payout: PayPal https://paypal.me/Jeremytsangchina\nBackup payout: USDT TRC20 `TWupTAoFjxR2VmqUUvzhfmUwXVZR6Kvz1Y`\nIf this specific program is RTC-only, please tell me the required wallet/miner-id format and I will provide it before payout.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/10984/reactions","total_count":10,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":2,"confused":0,"heart":2,"rocket":2,"eyes":2},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/10984/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/83","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Spectral-Finance/lux","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/83/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/83/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/83/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/83","id":2877968982,"node_id":"I_kwDONlDJhc6rilJW","number":83,"title":"Coinbase Exchange Integration $750","user":{"login":"rparcus","id":923630,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyMzYzMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/923630?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparcus","html_url":"https://github.com/rparcus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparcus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparcus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparcus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparcus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparcus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparcus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparcus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparcus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparcus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":8203667011,"node_id":"LA_kwDONlDJhc8AAAAB6PoGQw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Spectral-Finance/lux/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"395808","default":false,"description":""},{"id":8203948389,"node_id":"LA_kwDONlDJhc8AAAAB6P5RZQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Spectral-Finance/lux/labels/exchanges","name":"exchanges","color":"1D76DB","default":false,"description":"Exchange integrations and trading features"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":28,"created_at":"2025-02-25T10:44:17Z","updated_at":"2026-06-25T08:44:40Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Overview\n\nImplement Coinbase exchange integration for spot trading and advanced order management.\n\n## Core Features\n- REST API integration\n- WebSocket feeds\n- Order management\n- Market data streaming\n- Portfolio tracking\n- Account management\n- Historical data access\n- Rate limiting handling\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] REST API implementation\n- [ ] WebSocket integration\n- [ ] Order placement system\n- [ ] Market data handling\n- [ ] Account management features\n- [ ] Documentation and examples\n- [ ] Integration tests for trading operations\n- [ ] Rate limit compliance tests\n\n## Budget: \\$750","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/