4613547329,"node_id":"I_kwDOS0eC7s8AAAABEv0lQQ","number":2,"title":"Mission 11: ERC-7710 Liquid Democracy — Production Implementation","user":{"login":"jeremie-olivier","id":3015341,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMTUzNDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3015341?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremie-olivier","html_url":"https://github.com/jeremie-olivier","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremie-olivier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremie-olivier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremie-olivier/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremie-olivier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremie-olivier/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremie-olivier/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremie-olivier/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremie-olivier/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremie-olivier/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2026-06-08T14:01:32Z","updated_at":"2026-06-18T08:45:14Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**Board item:** ERC-7710 Liquid Democracy Production — Contracts + UI\n**Status:** Blocked | **Priority:** P0\n**Reward:** $3,000 USDC + iBox token\n**Target:** Solidity / full-stack developer with smart account and governance experience\n**Validation:** Hard requirement — Intuition Team must validate before payout\n**Chain:** Intuition Network (mainnet: 1155, testnet: 13579)\n**Prerequisite:** Mission 10 (POC) must be completed and validated first\n\n> ⚠️ **This mission is blocked.** It opens once [Mission 10](https://github.com/intuition-box/Liquid-Democracy/issues/1) is completed and validated by the Intuition Box core contributors.\n\n---\n\n## Context\n\nMission 10 delivers a proof-of-concept for ERC-7710 liquid democracy with Intuition graph domain caveats. This mission takes the POC to production: hardened contracts, a full-featured governance UI, and mainnet deployment.\n\nThe core mechanic (proven in Mission 10): a voter delegates their voting power scoped to a domain (e.g., `design`), and the caveat enforcer resolves that scope semantically via the Intuition knowledge graph — so a `branding` proposal automatically passes a `design`-scoped delegation because `branding - is a sub-domain of - design` exists onchain.\n\n## Objective\n\nShip a production-ready liquid democracy system on the Intuition chain: robust, auditable contracts with a full governance UI that any community could use to set up scoped delegation chains and vote on proposals.\n\n## Deliverables\n\n### Contracts\n\n- [ ] **Production Graph Domain Caveat Enforcer** — harden the POC enforcer:\n  - Chosen traversal approach solidified (onchain reads or proof-based — informed by POC writeup)\n  - Full snapshot/root hash support — graph state is captured at delegation time, recomputed and verified at enforcement time to prevent graph manipulation attacks\n  - Comprehensive edge case handling: circular graph paths, deleted atoms, type mismatches\n  - Gas-optimized traversal with clear documented limits\n  - Natspec documentation\n- [ ] **Delegation factory** — a contract that lets users create and manage delegation chains without raw calldata\n- [ ] **Audit-ready test suite** — 100% branch coverage, fuzz tests on traversal depth and caveat parameters, invariant tests on revocation\n\n### Frontend\n\n- [ ] **Delegation manager UI** — create, view, and revoke ERC-7710 delegations\n  - Connect wallet (wagmi + RainbowKit)\n  - Browse and select domain atoms from the Intuition graph as delegation scope\n  - Configure caveat parameters (depth, expiry, edge types)\n  - Visualize active delegation chains (who delegated what to whom)\n- [ ] **Governance UI** — submit and vote on proposals through delegated authority\n  - Create mock proposals with a declared domain\n  - Show in real time whether the connected account has (direct or delegated) authority to vote\n  - Display semantic resolution: why a proposal passed or failed the domain enforcer\n- [ ] **Domain graph explorer** — browse the Intuition knowledge graph to understand scope relationships\n  - Search atoms, traverse `is a sub-domain of` paths\n  - Show which domains are in scope for a given delegation\n- [ ] **Deployed on intuition.box subdomain** (TBD with team)\n\n### Documentation\n\n- [ ] Architecture doc: contracts, interfaces, trusted components, upgrade path\n- [ ] User guide: how to set up a delegation chain, how scope resolution works\n- [ ] Article / X thread for ecosystem announcement\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- All contracts deployed on Intuition mainnet (1155) and testnet (13579)\n- Enforcer passes a comprehensive audit-focused review (internal team review minimum)\n- Snapshot hash mechanism prevents graph manipulation — test suite proves it\n- Frontend is fully functional end-to-end with a real wallet on mainnet\n- A new user can set up a scoped delegation chain in under 5 minutes from the UI\n- Architecture doc is sufficient for the Intuition team to maintain and extend the system\n\n## Technical Notes\n\n- Build on the chosen approach from Mission 10 — do not reinvent; extend and harden\n- **Suggested contract stack:** Solidity 0.8.x + Foundry (fuzz + invariant tests)\n- **Suggested frontend stack:** React + wagmi v2 + RainbowKit + viem\n- Snapshot hashing design: at delegation time, hash the relevant subgraph (domain node + descendant edges within max depth); enforcer recomputes and compares — prevents an attacker from adding a malicious edge to the graph after delegation\n- The delegation factory should follow a pattern similar to Uniswap V2 factory for discoverability\n- Coordinate with the Intuition team on the canonical `is a sub-domain of` predicate and any existing domain atoms to reuse\n\n## Application\n\n**Step 1** — Comment on this issue explaining why you think you are a right fit for this mission and what excites you about it.\n\n**Step 2** — Contact **zet.box** on Discord to plan a call with the Intuition team.\n\n---\n\n## Open Questions\n\n- Should the production enforcer support pluggable edge types (any Intuition predicate can be a \"sub-domain\" relation), or should it be fixed to a single canonical predicate?\n- What's the upgrade/migration path from the POC testnet deployment?\n- Should the governance UI support a specific governor standard (OZ Governor, etc.) or remain mock-only for now?\n- Is there a target subdomain (e.g., `democracy.intuition.box`) for deployment?\n\n---\n\n*Prerequisite:* Mission 10 — ERC-7710 Liquid Democracy POC\n*Origin:* https://x.com/olivierjeremie/status/1925983073540370651\n*Related:* ERC-7710, Smart Account Kit, Intuition Knowledge Graph","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/intuition-box/Liquid-Democracy/issues/2/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/intuition-box/Liquid-Democracy/issues/2/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/55","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Spectral-Finance/lux","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/55/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/55/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/55/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/55","id":2877809097,"node_id":"I_kwDONlDJhc6rh-HJ","number":55,"title":"Agent Discord Capabilities ($500)","user":{"login":"rparcus","id":923630,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyMzYzMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/923630?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparcus","html_url":"https://github.com/rparcus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparcus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparcus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparcus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparcus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparcus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparcus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparcus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparcus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rparcus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":8203667011,"node_id":"LA_kwDONlDJhc8AAAAB6PoGQw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Spectral-Finance/lux/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"395808","default":false,"description":""}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":8,"created_at":"2025-02-25T09:50:52Z","updated_at":"2026-06-18T06:41:17Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# Agent Discord Behaviors\nImplement Prisms, Lenses and Beams so that an agent can perform basic operations in discord.\n\n- Server Management\n    - Join/leave servers\n    - Create/manage channels\n    - Manage roles and permissions\n    - Monitor server activities\n- Conversation Management\n    - Thread creation/management\n    - Message management\n    - Reaction handling\n    - Message history analysis\n- Role Management\n    - Role assignment\n    - Permission management\n    - Role hierarchy handling\n    - Custom role creation\n- Member Interaction\n    - Direct messaging\n    - Member management\n    - Activity monitoring\n    - User profiling\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n- Agent can fully manage server resources\n- Contextual conversation handling\n- Role-based behavior adaptation\n- Member interaction protocols\n- Comprehensive testing suite","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/55/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/55/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/canfieldjuan/ATLAS/issues/1656","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/canfieldjuan/ATLAS","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/canfieldjuan/ATLAS/issues/1656/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/canfieldjuan/ATLAS/issues/1656/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/canfieldjuan/ATLAS/issues/1656/events","html_url":"https://github.com/canfieldjuan/ATLAS/issues/1656","id":4679822436,"node_id":"I_kwDOQ5Uhrs8AAAABFvBsZA","number":1656,"title":"Security hardening (phase 2): RBAC, audit ledger, RLS, encryption, IR, deletion — beyond #1623","user":{"login":"canfieldjuan","id":17366102,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzY2MTAy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17366102?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/canfieldjuan","html_url":"https://github.com/canfieldjuan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canfieldjuan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canfieldjuan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canfieldjuan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canfieldjuan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canfieldjuan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canfieldjuan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canfieldjuan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canfieldjuan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canfieldjuan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":8,"created_at":"2026-06-17T03:44:25Z","updated_at":"2026-06-17T22:02:45Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Builds on #1623 (which landed the CI scanning baseline: gitleaks/Semgrep/Trivy/Checkov/pip-audit/OSV + Dependabot). This tracks the remaining **architecture & process** security gaps found in a full audit across both repos.\n\n**Companion (frontend/CI) issue:** canfieldjuan/atlas-portfolio (linked in a comment below). Shared cross-repo concerns are listed at the bottom and must be tackled holistically.\n\n### High\n- [ ] **Rotate exposed credentials** committed in `d63a9b77` (live-shaped Stripe/Anthropic/OpenRouter `.env`; flagged in the gitleaks baseline / `docs/SECURITY_GUARDRAILS.md`). Decide rotate vs history-rewrite. *(S)*\n- [ ] **Fix `blog_admin.py` authz** — `/admin/blog/*` is gated by `require_auth` only (any logged-in user), not admin role (`atlas_brain/api/blog_admin.py:270-1097`). *(S)*\n- [ ] **Backend report deletion + TTL** — `content_ops_deflection_reports` (migration `328`) has no delete path and no TTL, so the stored `snapshot`/`artifact` JSONB persists indefinitely. Add `delete_report(account_id, request_id)` to `deflection_report_access.py` + an authenticated endpoint + a 30-day TTL. **This is why the portfolio `/security` 30-day-deletion claim is currently false.** *(M)* — cross-repo, see below.\n\n### Medium\n- [ ] **Postgres RLS** on `content_ops_deflection_reports` + tenant tables (`SET app.account_id` per request). Isolation is currently app-level `WHERE account_id` only — one missing clause = cross-tenant leak. *(M-L)*\n- [ ] **App-level encryption** of `snapshot`/`artifact` JSONB by reusing the existing Fernet BYOK/rotation in `atlas_brain/auth/encryption.py:42-104` (already used for Zendesk creds, unused for deflection data). *(M)*\n- [ ] **Wire alert delivery to a real channel** — the paid-funnel incident pipeline (`alerts/manager.py:140`; 6 emit sites in `api/billing.py` L682/729/755/889/1012/1057) defaults to log-only, so money-path incidents never page a human. *(S)*\n- [ ] **Drop `?token=` query-param auth** (`atlas_brain/auth/dependencies.py:62`) — log/referrer leakage. *(S)*\n- [ ] **Ratchet scanners advisory -> blocking** — `docs/SECURITY_GUARDRAILS.md:23-24` documents that Semgrep/Trivy/Checkov/pip-audit/OSV are advisory + push-only. Burn down backlog, then run pip-audit/OSV on `pull_request` and drop `continue-on-error`/`exit-code:0`/`soft_fail`. *(M-L)*\n- [ ] **IR playbook** `docs/INCIDENT_RESPONSE.md` (SEV defs, on-call, comms, rotation, postmortem). *(M)*\n- [ ] **Structured JSON logging + error tracking** (Sentry/OTel for `atlas_brain`; currently plain stdout). *(M)*\n- [ ] **SECURITY.md + `/.well-known/security.txt`** disclosure policy (coordinate one contact across both repos). *(S)*\n- [ ] **CVE remediation SLA** (Critical 7d / High 30d / Moderate 90d) wired to Dependabot labels. *(M)*\n\n### Large / later (platform-coupled)\n- [ ] Granular RBAC (replace binary `is_admin`/`require_admin_user`). *(M)*\n- [ ] SSO/SAML + SCIM (e.g. WorkOS). *(L-XL)*\n- [ ] CMK over Postgres at-rest; EU data-residency deployment. *(L-XL)*\n- [ ] Centralized log aggregation + retention + WORM audit trail. *(L-XL)*\n- [ ] Public bug bounty — **gated** behind IR plan + disclosure policy existing first. *(XL)*\n\n---\n### Cross-repo / holistic (must move with the portfolio issue)\n1. **Deletion end-to-end** — ATLAS delete endpoint + TTL (above) <-> portfolio `gap-report-cleanup` must call it + fix `security/page.tsx` copy. Neither side honors the 30-day promise alone.\n2. **Stripe/payment integrity** — ATLAS `billing.py` (checkout authorization, webhook unlock, amount/currency gate) <-> portfolio `deflection-checkout.ts` (session creation, allowed-amount re-check). Keep preflight==runtime and the two-env amount allowlist in sync on any change.\n3. **Tenant isolation / `request_id` capability** — the public funnel saves all customers under one shared service `account_id` (`control_surfaces.py` ~3277/3300), separated only by the portfolio-minted `request_id`. RLS (ATLAS) + request_id unguessability (portfolio) are a joint design.\n4. **Encryption of customer ticket content** — portfolio uploads CSV to Blob <-> ATLAS stores derived JSONB. At-rest encryption is one data-path decision.\n5. **Secret rotation** — the exposed `.env` (Stripe/Anthropic/etc.) keys are consumed in both repos; rotation must cover both consumers.\n6. **Disclosure policy** — one coordinated SECURITY.md/security.txt contact across both repos.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/canfieldjuan/ATLAS/issues/1656/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/canfieldjuan/ATLAS/issues/1656/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spaceandtimefdn/sxt-proof-of-sql/issues/229","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spaceandtimefdn/sxt-proof-of-sql","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spaceandtimefdn/sxt-proof-of-sql/issues/229/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spaceandtimefdn/sxt-proof-of-sql/issues/229/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spaceandtimefdn/sxt-proof-of-sql/issues/229/events","html_url":"https://github.com/spaceandtimefdn/sxt-proof-of-sql/issues/229","id":2569967536,"node_id":"I_kwDOLzQ-MM6ZLpew","number":229,"title":"Add `FixedSizeBinary` with support up to at least 32 bytes.","user":{"login":"JayWhite2357","id":7530828,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MzA4Mjg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7530828?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JayWhite2357","html_url":"https://github.com/JayWhite2357","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JayWhite2357/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JayWhite2357/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JayWhite2357/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JayWhite2357/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JayWhite2357/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JayWhite2357/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JayWhite2357/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JayWhite2357/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JayWhite2357/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":6871673924,"node_id":"LA_kwDOLzQ-MM8AAAABmZVsRA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spaceandtimefdn/sxt-proof-of-sql/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","color":"a2eeef","default":true,"description":"New feature or request"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"Dustin-Ray","id":40841027,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwODQxMDI3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40841027?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dustin-Ray","html_url":"https://github.com/Dustin-Ray","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dustin-Ray/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dustin-Ray/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dustin-Ray/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dustin-Ray/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dustin-Ray/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dustin-Ray/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dustin-Ray/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dustin-Ray/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dustin-Ray/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":25,"created_at":"2024-10-07T10:08:01Z","updated_at":"2026-06-17T18:23:40Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":{"login":"Dustin-Ray","id":40841027,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwODQxMDI3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40841027?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dustin-Ray","html_url":"https://github.com/Dustin-Ray","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dustin-Ray/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dustin-Ray/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dustin-Ray/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dustin-Ray/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dustin-Ray/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dustin-Ray/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dustin-Ray/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dustin-Ray/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dustin-Ray/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# Background and Motivation\r\n\r\nMany data are binary blobs. In particular, the EVM address and hash types are 20 bytes and 32 bytes respectively. We should support these natively within Proof of SQL. See https://docs.rs/arrow/latest/arrow/datatypes/enum.DataType.html#variant.FixedSizeBinary.\r\n\r\n# Changes Requested\r\n\r\nAdd full support for a `FixedSizeBinary` type. In order to do this there are several considerations.\r\n* Since `Scalar` types support naturally embedding 31 bytes but not 32 bytes, there should be a divergence in how <=31 bytes are handled and 32 bytes are handled.\r\n    * 31 bytes and under should be naturally embedded into the `Scalar` type. This means simply relying on the conversion from `[u64; 4]` to the `Scalar`.\r\n    * 32 bytes should be handled by first hashing the data and then converting it to a `Scalar`. This is identical to how `String`s are handled. See https://github.com/spaceandtimelabs/sxt-proof-of-sql/blob/48b2f0bc8b92dbc3ef9deecfdfc04dfbc2b4460c/crates/proof-of-sql/src/base/scalar/mont_scalar_from.rs#L16.\r\n* `ColumnType` should probably have a new variant `FixedSizeBinary(i32)` added. It is not as clear what the variant for `Column` and `OwnedColumn` should be.\r\n    * My initial suggestion would be `FixedSizeBinary(i32, &'a [u8])` and `FixedSizeBinary(i32, Vec<u8>)` respectively, but that may not make sense. The reason for this suggestion is because something like `Vec<Vec<u8>>` has a lot of overhead, and `Vec<[u8]>` is not allowed by Rust.\r\n    * Alternatively, it may make sense to have two variants: one for the <=31 bytes case, and one for the 32 bytes case. In this case, it may make sense to have the latter simply be `Binary` instead of `FixedSizeBinary`.\r\n* #228 is partially motivated by this issue, and may make this issue a bit more ergonomic. However, working on them in parallel will likely lead to some branch conflict, so pay attention to that issue.\r\n* The only expression that needs to be supported is equality (`=`) and inequality (`!=`). This is because there is no way to add, subtract, etc. between binary data. Eventually, we may wish to add bitwise operations, but those are beyond the scope of this issue.\r\n* It is not clear what the best way to handle binary literals is. We strive to adhere to PostgreSQL syntax, but this data type is unsupported in PostgreSQL. See https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/datatype-binary.html. There is some flexibility here, but there should be agreement on this before this particular implementation is done.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spaceandtimefdn/sxt-proof-of-sql/issues/229/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spaceandtimefdn/sxt-proof-of-sql/issues/229/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/bottube/issues/1411","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/bottube","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/bottube/issues/1411/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/bottube/issues/1411/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/bottube/issues/1411/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/bottube/issues/1411","id":4652375715,"node_id":"I_kwDORFt8-M8AAAABFU2eow","number":1411,"title":"[BUG] /discover returns HTTP 500 (Server Error) — search_blueprint discover_page() crashes","user":{"login":"jdjioe5-cpu","id":257431731,"node_id":"U_kgDOD1gYsw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257431731?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu","html_url":"https://github.com/jdjioe5-cpu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":18,"created_at":"2026-06-12T20:25:49Z","updated_at":"2026-06-17T17:02:45Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Summary\n\n`https://bottube.ai/discover` redirects (308) to `/discover/` which returns HTTP 500 with the in-app Flask 500 template. The route exists (registered by `search_blueprint.py:search_bp` at `url_prefix=/discover`, with `discover_page()` mapped to `/`).\n\n## Live verification (2026-06-13T04:25 CST)\n\n```\n$ curl -sI https://bottube.ai/discover\nHTTP/2 308\nlocation: http://bottube.ai/discover/\n\n$ curl -sI https://bottube.ai/discover/\nHTTP/2 500\ncontent-type: text/html\ntitle: 500 - Server Error - AI Video Platform\n```\n\nBody shows the in-app Flask 500 template (no upstream nginx error). This is a Python-side crash.\n\n## Source analysis\n\n`search_blueprint.py:15` declares:\n```python\nsearch_bp = Blueprint(\"search\", __name__, url_prefix=\"/discover\")\n```\n\n`search_blueprint.py:57-60`:\n```python\n@search_bp.route(\"/\")\ndef discover_page():\n    \"\"\"Main discoverability page with search, filters, and trending.\"\"\"\n    return render_template(\"discover.html\", categories=VIDEO_CATEGORIES)\n```\n\n`bottube_templates/discover.html` exists (20632 bytes).\n\nSo the route exists, the template exists, but the response is a Flask 500. The most likely causes (in priority order):\n1. `VIDEO_CATEGORIES` import missing or runtime error.\n2. Template render error (template references variables not in context).\n3. Deployment drift (production is on an older `bottube_server.py` that registers the blueprint differently or with a bug).\n\n## Impact\n\nMedium. `/discover` is the canonical discovery surface; breaking it makes the platform look broken to first-time visitors who follow the search/discover entry point.\n\n## Suggested action\n\nCheck the live `bottube.ai` Flask logs for the 500 traceback. The fix is either a small `discover.html` template variable add or a re-deploy of `main` (last clean merge `3d57339`).","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/bottube/issues/1411/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/bottube/issues/1411/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dev-kp-eloper/BountyScout/issues/233","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dev-kp-eloper/BountyScout","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dev-kp-eloper/BountyScout/issues/233/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dev-kp-eloper/BountyScout/issues/233/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dev-kp-eloper/BountyScout/issues/233/events","html_url":"https://github.com/dev-kp-eloper/BountyScout/issues/233","id":4682952409,"node_id":"I_kwDOSmCMss8AAAABFyAu2Q","number":233,"title":"🎯 Bounty Alert: 22 New Opportunityies found","user":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/i