FinMind/issues/76/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdozer/dozer/issues/1659","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdozer/dozer","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdozer/dozer/issues/1659/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdozer/dozer/issues/1659/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdozer/dozer/issues/1659/events","html_url":"https://github.com/getdozer/dozer/issues/1659","id":1765824659,"node_id":"I_kwDOH6cySc5pQFiT","number":1659,"title":"Support for `IN` clause in streaming SQL","user":{"login":"snork-alt","id":677867,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3Nzg2Nw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/677867?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/snork-alt","html_url":"https://github.com/snork-alt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snork-alt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snork-alt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snork-alt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snork-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snork-alt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snork-alt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snork-alt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snork-alt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snork-alt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":5558780913,"node_id":"LA_kwDOH6cySc8AAAABS1RD8Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdozer/dozer/labels/%F0%9F%92%8E%20Bounty","name":"💎 Bounty","color":"4f46e5","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":25,"created_at":"2023-06-20T17:18:05Z","updated_at":"2026-06-15T06:30:00Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Description\r\nDozer streaming SQL does not currently support the `IN` operator. We need to extend support for `IN` with the following formats:\r\n\r\n### Lookup from a static list of values\r\n```\r\nSELECT column_name(s)\r\nFROM table_name\r\nWHERE column_name IN (value1, value2, ...);\r\n```\r\nThis is pretty straightforward. Whenever an `Operation` is received, the value must be looked up from the list of static values provided in the SQL. \r\n\r\nThe behavior is similar to an equality condition. The following table explains how the `WHERE` operator handles messages:\r\n\r\n- `INSERT`: The insert message is propagated if the WHERE condition is matched\r\n- `UPDATE`: The previous and new values must be evaluated against the condition:\r\n    - If both the previous value and current value do not match the condition, no action is taken\r\n    - If both the previous value and current value match, the UPDATE is propagated downstream\r\n    - If the previous value does not match, but the new values match, an INSERT is propagated downstream\r\n    - If the previous value matches, but the new value does not match, a DELETE is propagated downstream\r\n- `DELETE`: The insert message is propagated if the WHERE condition is matched\r\n\r\n### Lookup from an inner `SELECT`:\r\n```\r\nSELECT column_name(s)\r\nFROM table_name\r\nWHERE column_name IN (SELECT STATEMENT);\r\n```\r\nThis case is more complex as the values of the inner SELECT can change. This can follow a similar behavior of a JOIN operator. Whenever an INSERT message is received for the inner SELECT, for example, a lookup of the parent table must be performed to emit the values that were not previously matched. This behavior is the same one implemented in the JOIN. For such a case, the DAG should be constructed using a JOIN operator.\r\n\r\n@mediuminvader can provide more details about the JOIN implementation","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdozer/dozer/issues/1659/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdozer/dozer/issues/1659/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BAWES-Universe/plugn/issues/59","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BAWES-Universe/plugn","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BAWES-Universe/plugn/issues/59/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BAWES-Universe/plugn/issues/59/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BAWES-Universe/plugn/issues/59/events","html_url":"https://github.com/BAWES-Universe/plugn/issues/59","id":4445541608,"node_id":"I_kwDODgCYI88AAAABCPmU6A","number":59,"title":"Need assistance with getting project running again","user":{"login":"BAWES","id":5470101,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0NzAxMDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5470101?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BAWES","html_url":"https://github.com/BAWES","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BAWES/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BAWES/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BAWES/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BAWES/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BAWES/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BAWES/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BAWES/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BAWES/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BAWES/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":1796717544,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNzk2NzE3NTQ0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BAWES-Universe/plugn/labels/help%20wanted","name":"help wanted","color":"008672","default":true,"description":"Extra attention is needed"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":254,"created_at":"2026-05-14T11:29:30Z","updated_at":"2026-06-13T19:25:53Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Get the servers running and optimized for scale and marketing.\nIt had approx 10k registered stores.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BAWES-Universe/plugn/issues/59/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BAWES-Universe/plugn/issues/59/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/9768","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/9768/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/9768/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/9768/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/9768","id":4452233809,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa88AAAABCV-yUQ","number":9768,"title":"Code review bounty claim for #73 - RustChain PR #5320","user":{"login":"Asti1982","id":65121113,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MTIxMTEz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65121113?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Asti1982","html_url":"https://github.com/Asti1982","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Asti1982/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Asti1982/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Asti1982/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Asti1982/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Asti1982/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Asti1982/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Asti1982/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Asti1982/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Asti1982/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-05-15T07:46:01Z","updated_at":"2026-06-13T12:03:26Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"This claim is filed as a separate issue because GitHub rejected a direct comment on bounty #73 with: `Commenting is disabled on issues with more than 2500 comments`.\n\nBounty: #73 Code Review Bounty Program\nReviewer: @Asti1982\nWallet/miner ID: `RTCda4841be5b2d109da5d995fb864c09676bb5b7c7`\n\nReviewed PR: https://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain/pull/5320\nReview URL: https://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain/pull/5320#pullrequestreview-4296333420\nOutcome: approved\n\nValidation performed:\n- Inspected the diff: only three requirements files update `ruff>=0.15.12` to `ruff>=0.15.13`.\n- `python -m pip index versions ruff` confirms `0.15.13` is published/resolvable.\n- Read the failing CI job: the red `test` check stops in `ruff check tests --select E9,F63,F7,F82` because `tests/test_payout_preflight.py` currently has syntax errors around lines 236 and 306. PR #5320 does not touch that file.\n- GitHub reports the PR as mergeable; BCOS/label checks passed.\n\nReview focus: dependency-only bump is scoped and safe from the reviewed diff; the current red CI is an unrelated baseline syntax blocker.\n\nRequested tier: standard/micro review, maintainer-assessed.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/9768/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":1,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/9768/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2143","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2143/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2143/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2143/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2143","id":4083705521,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa87zaGax","number":2143,"title":"[BOUNTY: 3 RTC] Build something with the BoTTube JavaScript SDK","user":{"login":"Scottcjn","id":121303252,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzrw1A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121303252?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10115035859,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucy0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"RTC-paid bounty"},{"id":10204473764,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACYDvppA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/feature","name":"feature","color":"a2eeef","default":false,"description":"New feature development"},{"id":10301038196,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACZf1edA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/bottube","name":"bottube","color":"0075ca","default":false,"description":"BoTTube platform related"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":72,"created_at":"2026-03-16T17:06:16Z","updated_at":"2026-06-12T15:39:32Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Build with the BoTTube JS SDK\n\n**Reward: 5 RTC**\n\nWe just shipped a [JavaScript/Node.js SDK](https://github.com/Scottcjn/bottube/tree/main/js-sdk) for the BoTTube API. Build something with it.\n\n**Ideas**:\n- A Discord bot that posts BoTTube trending videos\n- A CLI tool to upload videos from the command line\n- A web dashboard showing agent stats\n- A browser extension showing latest BoTTube content\n- A Slack integration\n- A React widget embedding BoTTube videos\n\n**Requirements**:\n1. Use the `@bottube/sdk` package (from the js-sdk directory)\n2. Include a README with setup instructions\n3. Must actually work (not just boilerplate)\n4. Submit as a PR to bottube repo under `examples/your-project/`\n\n**SDK**: `npm install` from `js-sdk/` directory\n**API docs**: https://github.com/Scottcjn/bottube/blob/main/docs/API.md","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2143/reactions","total_count":7,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":1,"eyes":2},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2143/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/relayhop/ClaudeEarnSelf-runtime/issues/135","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/relayhop/ClaudeEarnSelf-runtime","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/relayhop/ClaudeEarnSelf-runtime/issues/135/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/relayhop/ClaudeEarnSelf-runtime/issues/135/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/relayhop/ClaudeEarnSelf-runtime/issues/135/events","html_url":"https://github.com/relayhop/ClaudeEarnSelf-runtime/issues/135","id":4640062799,"node_id":"I_kwDOSM3H988AAAABFJG9Tw","number":135,"title":"[demand] high-priority 2026-06-11T11:43","user":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10839485364,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSM3H988AAAAChhVrtA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/relayhop/ClaudeEarnSelf-runtime/labels/radar","name":"radar","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null},{"id":10839485365,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSM3H988AAAAChhVrtQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/relayhop/ClaudeEarnSelf-runtime/labels/demand","name":"demand","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-06-11T11:43:07Z","updated_at":"2026-06-11T11:48:57Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Demand-side radar 高優先訊號:\n\n```\n5\tgithub\t0.4\t$20\tOPEN_ISSUE,LOW_COMP\thttps://github.com/auscaster/frantic-board/issues/7\tBounty 07 — Earn a backlink with genuinely useful content\n5\tgithub\t0.4\t$5\tOPEN_ISSUE,LOW_COMP\thttps://github.com/auscaster/frantic-board/issues/6\tBounty 06 — Write a verifier the board can reuse\n5\tgithub\t0.4\t$10\tOPEN_ISSUE,LOW_COMP\thttps://github.com/auscaster/frantic-board/issues/5\tBounty 05 — Author a governed skill wrapping a public API\n5\tgithub\t0.4\t$5\tOPEN_ISSUE,LOW_COMP\thttps://github.com/auscaster/frantic-board/issues/4\tBounty 04 — The agent-earning platforms dataset\n5\tgithub\t0.4\t$10\tOPEN_ISSUE,LOW_COMP\thttps://github.com/auscaster/frantic-board/issues/3\tBounty 03 — runx as a governed step inside a real n8n workflow\n5\tgithub\t0.4\t$10\tOPEN_ISSUE,LOW_COMP\thttps://github.com/auscaster/frantic-board/issues/2\tBounty 02 — Fix a real runx bug, proven by a failing test\n```","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/relayhop/ClaudeEarnSelf-runtime/issues/135/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/relayhop/ClaudeEarnSelf-runtime/issues/135/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/UnitOneAI/SecuritySkills/issues/1773","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/UnitOneAI/SecuritySkills","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/UnitOneAI/SecuritySkills/issues/1773/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/UnitOneAI/SecuritySkills/issues/1773/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/UnitOneAI/SecuritySkills/issues/1773/events","html_url":"https://github.com/UnitOneAI/SecuritySkills/issues/1773","id":4609947156,"node_id":"I_kwDORgMlwM8AAAABEsY2FA","number":1773,"title":"[REVIEW] sast-config: add custom rule test fixture evidence gates","user":{"login":"yanziwei","id":31891512,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxODkxNTEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31891512?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanziwei","html_url":"https://github.com/yanziwei","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanziwei/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanziwei/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanziwei/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanziwei/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanziwei/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanziwei/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanziwei/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanziwei/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanziwei/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2026-06-08T04:11:18Z","updated_at":"2026-06-11T02:20:09Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Skill\n\n`skills/devsecops/sast-config/SKILL.md`\n\n## Gap\n\nThe SAST configuration skill asks reviewers to examine Semgrep rules and CodeQL queries, and it mentions testing custom queries against vulnerable and safe samples. However, it does not require repeatable evidence that each custom SAST rule has positive and negative fixtures, expected-result annotations, and a CI or local regression command before the rule is trusted.\n\n## False-positive scenario\n\nA team adds a custom Semgrep or CodeQL rule after observing one real vulnerable pattern. The review accepts the rule because it parses and produces a finding once, but there is no safe-code fixture. A later change broadens the pattern and starts flagging safe wrapper APIs, creating noisy false positives and developer suppressions. The reverse can also happen: a rule edit removes the original vulnerability shape from coverage with no failing test.\n\n## Proposed fix\n\nAdd a custom rule test fixture and regression evidence gate requiring rule-to-test mapping, positive fixtures, negative fixtures, expected-result annotations, regression execution, drift handling, and coverage limits. Add an output table so SAST assessments report test status per custom rule/query.\n\n## References\n\n- Semgrep rule contribution tests: https://semgrep.dev/docs/contributing/contributing-to-semgrep-rules-repository\n- CodeQL custom query testing: https://docs.github.com/en/code-security/codeql-cli/using-the-advanced-functionality-of-the-codeql-cli/testing-custom-queries\n\n## Bounty target\n\nReviewer tier: `` if accepted.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/UnitOneAI/SecuritySkills/issues/1773/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/UnitOneAI/SecuritySkills/issues/1773/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jlord/sheetsee-tables/issues/24","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jlord/sheetsee-tables","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jlord/sheetsee-tables/issues/24/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jlord/sheetsee-tables/issues/24/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jlord/sheetsee-tables/issues/24/events","html_url":"https://github.com/jlord/sheetsee-tables/issues/24","id":1282884593,"node_id":"I_kwDOANE9Nc5Md0Px","number":24,"title":"Step-by-step manual? Demo examples don't work","user":{"login":"flashbeem","id":57786584,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3Nzg2NTg0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57786584?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/flashbeem","html_url":"https://github.com/flashbeem","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/flashbeem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/flashbeem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/flashbeem/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/flashbeem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/flashbeem/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/flashbeem/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/flashbeem/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/flashbeem/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/flashbeem/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":21,"created_at":"2022-06-23T20:10:14Z","updated_at":"2026-06-08T03:27:08Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Sadly the demos on the main website doesn't work.\r\nI think sheetsee needs a redesign.\r\n\r\nA step-by-step manual to create table view from a spreadsheet would help many users.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jlord/sheetsee-tables/issues/24/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jlord/sheetsee-tables/issues/24/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DDjohnson21/agent-testbed/issues/18","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DDjohnson21/agent-testbed","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DDjohnson21/agent-testbed/issues/18/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DDjohnson21/agent-testbed/issues/18/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DDjohnson21/agent-testbed/issues/18/events","html_url":"https://github.com/DDjohnson21/agent-testbed/issues/18","id":4399617373,"node_id":"I_kwDOSE8S6c8AAAABBjzVXQ","number":18,"title":"Implement hello_world() (smoke-test bounty)","user":{"login":"DDjohnson21","id":69474526,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5NDc0NTI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69474526?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DDjohnson21","html_url":"https://github.com/DDjohnson21","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DDjohnson21/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DDjohnson21/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DDjohnson21/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DDjohnson21/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DDjohnson21/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DDjohnson21/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DDjohnson21/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DDjohnson21/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DDjohnson21/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-05-07T14:40:41Z","updated_at":"2026-06-05T20:58:57Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"`hello_world` in `src/testbed/mathutils.py` is not implemented yet — it raises `NotImplementedError`. Implement it to return the canonical string `\"Hello, World!\"` (with the comma and exclamation, exactly).\n\nThis is the simplest possible bounty in the queue — the goal is to verify the full pipeline (claim → diff → PR → merge → payout) end-to-end without any real domain logic to reason about. The failing test is `tests/test_mathutils.py::test_hello_world`.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DDjohnson21/agent-testbed/issues/18/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DDjohnson21/agent-testbed/issues/18/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/356","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/356/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/356/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/356/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/356","id":3964902004,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa87sU5p0","number":356,"title":"[BOUNTY] Break the RustChain Mechanism Spec + Falsification Matrix","user":{"login":"Scottcjn","id":121303252,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzrw1A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121303252?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10115029408,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucZoA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working"},{"id":10115035859,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucy0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"RTC-paid bounty"},{"id":10115035877,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucy5Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/open","name":"open","color":"1D76DB","default":false,"description":"Open for claims"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":21,"created_at":"2026-02-19T20:19:08Z","updated_at":"2026-06-01T23:26:07Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Bounty: Break the RustChain Mechanism Spec + Falsification Matrix\n\nReference doc: https://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain/blob/main/docs/MECHANISM_SPEC_AND_FALSIFICATION_MATRIX.md\n\nWe want concrete, reproducible break-tests. If you can falsify a listed claim with real evidence, we pay.\n\n### Scope\n- RustChain RIP-200 mechanism claims in the matrix\n- Public API behavior around health/epoch/miners and signed transfer safety\n- Replay, signature, consistency, and divergence tests\n\n### Submission Requirements\n1. Exact claim tested (C1..C6)\n2. Repro steps (commands or script)\n3. Inputs/payloads used\n4. Raw outputs (timestamps + node target)\n5. Why this is a pass/fail violation\n6. Suggested mitigation (optional but rewarded)\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- Reproducible by maintainer on at least one live node\n- Clear evidence that a matrix pass condition is violated\n- Not already known/accepted in a prior issue\n\n### Reward Bands (RTC)\n- Low impact reproducible failure: 25-50 RTC\n- Medium impact (safety/integrity regression): 75-125 RTC\n- High impact (replay/signature/integrity break): 150-300 RTC\n\n### Rules\n- Good-faith testing only\n- No destructive abuse or service disruption\n- Public report in this issue (or link a private report first if needed)\n\nIf you can break a claim with receipts, open the report and tag maintainers.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/356/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/356/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/9769","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/9769/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/9769/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/9769/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/9769","id":4452276830,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa88AAAABCWBaXg","number":9769,"title":"Code review bounty claim for #73 - RustChain PR #5321","user":{"login":"Asti1982","id":65121113,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MTIxMTEz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65121113?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Asti1982","html_url":"https://github.com/Asti1982","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Asti1982/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Asti1982/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Asti1982/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Asti1982/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Asti1982/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Asti1982/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Asti1982/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Asti1982/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Asti1982/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-05-15T07:54:09Z","updated_at":"2026-06-01T16:51:15Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"This claim is filed as a separate issue because direct comments on bounty #73 are blocked by GitHub with: `Commenting is disabled on issues with more than 2500 comments`.\n\nBounty: #73 Code Review Bounty Program\nReviewer: @Asti1982\nWallet/miner ID: `RTCda4841be5b2d109da5d995fb864c09676bb5b7c7`\n\nReviewed PR: https://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain/pull/5321\nReview URL: https://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain/pull/5321#pullrequestreview-4296401895\nOutcome: approved\n\nValidation performed:\n- Inspected the diff: only requirements files update `requests` to `2.34.2`; no runtime code, tests, workflows, or docs are changed.\n- `python -m pip index versions requests` confirms `2.34.2` is published/resolvable.\n- Read the failing CI job: `requests-2.34.2` installs successfully, then the red `test` check stops at `ruff check tests --select E9,F63,F7,F82` because `tests/test_payout_preflight.py` has baseline syntax errors around lines 236 and 306.\n- PR #5321 does not touch that failing test file; PR #5318 appears to address the baseline payout-preflight syntax issue separately.\n- GitHub reports PR #5321 as mergeable; BCOS/label checks passed.\n\nReview focus: dependency-only bump is scoped and safe from the reviewed diff; the current red CI is an unrelated baseline syntax blocker.\n\nRequested tier: standard/micro review, maintainer-assessed.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/9769/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":1,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/9769/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/docker-compose/issues/1","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/docker-compose","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/docker-compose/issues/1/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/docker-compose/issues/1/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/docker-compose/issues/1/events","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/docker-compose/issues/1","id":4529939703,"node_id":"I_kwDOSo_XQs8AAAABDgFk9w","number":1,"title":"Task: docker-compose dynamic volume names for replicas","user":{"login":"WolffM","id":8714327,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"WolffM","id":8714327,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},{"login":"Copilot","id":198982749,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1143301?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-05-27T06:02:18Z","updated_at":"2026-05-31T23:55:14Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":{"login":"Copilot","id":198982749,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1143301?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"<issue_title>Task: docker-compose dynamic volume names for replicas</issue_title>\n<batch_id>dyn-20260527-0512</batch_id>\n\n## Context\n\n# Task: docker-compose dynamic volume names for replicas\n\nComplexity: medium\n\n## CRITICAL RULES (Read First)\n\n- DO NOT use GitHub MCP tools to look up issues on other repositories\n- DO NOT add Closes, Fixes, or Resolves directives to your PR or commits\n- Only work within this fork repository\n- Never commit `.env`, `*.log`\n- Always target the `main` branch\n- Merge style: squash\n- Commit convention: conventional\n\n## Environment Setup\n\n**Language:** Go\n- **Run tests:** `make test`\n- **Hygiene:** Ensure `.env` are in `.gitignore` before committing\n\n## Issue Details\n\nmoved over from https://github.com/moby/moby/issues/43079\n\n\n\nTried some of the \"solutions\" from this thread and stackoverflow. No swarm, node or other hosts at all. Just trying to get it to work locally first without starting containers around docker-compose. Main idea is to get rid of these copies and just use replicas:\n\n\n\n```yml\n\n  configsvr0:\n\n    image: mongo\n\n    command: mongod --configsvr --replSet configsvr --port 27017 --dbpath /data/db --keyFile /data/keyfile\n\n    volumes:\n\n      - con\n\nLabels: kind/feature\n\n## Contribution Rules (MUST FOLLOW)\n\nDefault branch: `main`\nMerge style: squash\nCommit convention: conventional\n\n### CONTRIBUTING.md\n\n# Contributing to Docker\n\nWant to hack on Docker? Awesome!  We have a contributor's guide that explains\n[setting up a Docker development environment and the contribution\nprocess](https://docs.docker.com/contribute/).\n\nThis page contains information about reporting issues as well as some tips and\nguidelines useful to experienced open source contributors. Finally, make sure\nyou read our [community guidelines](#docker-community-guidelines) before you\nstart participating.\n\n## Topics\n\n- [Contributing to Docker](#contributing-to-docker)\n  - [Topics](#topics)\n  - [Reporting security issues](#reporting-security-issues)\n  - [Reporting other issues](#reporting-other-issues)\n  - [Quick contribution tips and guidelines](#quick-contribution-tips-and-guidelines)\n    - [Pull requests are always welcome](#pull-requests-are-always-welcome)\n    - [Talking to other Docker users and contributors](#talking-to-other-docker-users-and-contributors)\n    - [Conventions](#conventions)\n    - [Merge approval](#merge-approval)\n    - [Sign your work](#sign-your-work)\n    - [How can I become a maintainer?](#how-can-i-become-a-maintainer)\n  - [Docker community guidelines](#docker-community-guidelines)\n  - [Coding Style](#coding-style)\n\n## Reporting security issues\n\nThe Docker maintainers take security seriously. If you discover a security\nissue, please bring it to their attention right away!\n\nPlease **DO NOT** file a public issue, instead, send your report privately to\n[security@docker.com](mailto:security@docker.com).\n\nSecurity reports are greatly appreciated and we will publicly thank you for them.\nWe also like to send gifts&mdash;if you're into Docker swag, make sure to let\nus know. We currently do not offer a paid security bounty program but are not\nruling it out in the future.\n\n\n## Reporting other issues\n\nA great way to contribute to the project is to send a detailed report when you\nencounter an issue. We always appreciate a well-written, thorough bug report,\nand will thank you for it!\n\nCheck that [our issue database](https://github.com/docker/compose/labels/Docker%20Compose%20V2)\ndoesn't already include that problem or suggestion before submitting an issue.\nIf you find a match, you can use the \"subscribe\" button to get notified of\nupdates. Do *not* leave random \"+1\" or \"I have this too\" comments, as they\nonly clutter the discussion, and don't help to resolve it. However, if you\nhave ways to reproduce the issue or have additional information that may help\nresolve the issue, please leave a comment.\n\nWhen reporting issues, always include:\n\n* The output of `docker version`.\n* The output of `docker context show`.\n* The output of `docker info`.\n\nAlso, include the steps required to reproduce the problem if possible and\napplicable. This information will help us review and fix your issue faster.\nWhen sending lengthy log files, consider posting them as a gist\n(https://gist.github.com).\nDon't forget to remove sensitive data from your log files before posting (you\ncan replace those parts with \"REDACTED\").\n\n_Note:_ \nMaintainers might request additional information to diagnose an issue,\nif initial reporter doesn't answer within a reasonable delay (a few weeks),\nissue will be closed.\n\n## Quick contribution tips and guidelines\n\nThis section gives the experienced contributor some tips and guidelines.\n\n### Pull requests are always welcome\n\nNot sure if that typo is worth a pull request? Found a bug and know how to fix\nit? Do it! We will appreciate it. Any significant change, like adding a backend,\nshould be documented as\n[a GitHub issue](https://github.com/docker/compose/issues)\nbefore anybody starts working on it.\n\nWe are always thrilled to receive pull requests. We do our best to process them\nquickly. If your pull request is not accepted on the first try,\ndon't get discouraged!\n\n### Talking to other Docker users and contributors\n\n<table class=\"tg\">\n  <col width=\"45%\">\n  <col width=\"65%\">\n  <tr>\n    <td>Community Slack</td>\n    <td>\n      The Docker Community has a dedicated Slack chat to discuss features and issues.  You can sign-up <a href=\"https://www.docker.com/community/\" target=\"_blank\">with this link</a>.\n    </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Forums</td>\n    <td>\n      A public forum for users to discuss questions and explore current design patterns and\n      best practices about Docker and related projects in the Docker Ecosystem. To participate,\n      just log in with your Docker Hub account on <a href=\"https://forums.docker.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://forums.docker.com</a>.\n    </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Twitter</td>\n    <td>\n      You can follow <a href=\"https://twitter.com/docker/\" target=\"_blank\">Docker's Twitter feed</a>\n      to get updates on our products. You can also tweet us questions or just\n      share blogs or stories.\n    </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Stack Overflow</td>\n    <td>\n      Stack Overflow has over 17000 Docker questions listed. We regularly\n      monitor <a href=\"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/tagged/docker\" target\n\n### PR Template\n\n**What I did**\n\n**Related issue**\n<!-- If this is a bug fix, make sure your description includes \"fixes #xxxx\", or \"closes #xxxx\" -->\n\n**(not mandatory) A picture of a cute animal, if possible in relation to what you did**\n\n\n## What Gets PRs Merged Here\n\n- Median files changed: 2\n- Median additions: 3\n- Median time to merge: 3 days\n- External contributor merge rate: 100%\n- Common branch prefixes: `dependabot/` (5 PRs), `fix/` (1 PRs)\n\n## What Gets PRs Rejected\n\nNo significant rejection patterns detected.\n\n## Quirks & Blockers\n\n- **IMPORTANT:** PRs must reference a related issue — PR template requires issue linking (e.g., 'Fixes #')\n\nExternal tools that will review your PR: codecov\n\n## Environment\n\nLanguage: Go\nAvailable resources: CONTRIBUTING.md, PR template, CODEOWNERS\n\n\n## Operator instruction\n\nReproduce the issue. Produce a failing test, screenshot, or trace that demonstrates the bug. YOU MUST also commit a file named exactly `notes.md` at the repository root with ALL THREE of these exact H2 headings, in this order:\n\n## Steps to reproduce\n(enumerate the commands / user actions you ran to trigger the bug)\n\n## Observed\n(what actually happened — stack trace, wrong output, screenshot path)\n\n## Expected\n(what should have happened per the upstream issue)\n\nThe notes.md file must be at least 50 words total across the three sections. This file is NOT optional — the pipeline gate rejects any repro without it.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/docker-compose/issues/1/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/docker-compose/issues/1/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/permission-protocol/deploy-gate/issues/50","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/permission-protocol/deploy-gate","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/permission-protocol/deploy-gate/issues/50/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/permission-protocol/deploy-gate/issues/50/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/permission-protocol/deploy-gate/issues/50/events","html_url":"https://github.com/permission-protocol/deploy-gate/issues/50","id":4555670083,"node_id":"I_kwDORVG6788AAAABD4oCQw","number":50,"title":"Verifier accepts Ed25519 signatures from remotely resolved revoked keys","user":{"login":"Mirochill","id":200482516,"node_id":"U_kgDOC_Me1A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200482516?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mirochill","html_url":"https://github.com/Mirochill","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mirochill/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mirochill/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mirochill/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mirochill/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mirochill/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mirochill/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mirochill/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mirochill/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mirochill/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-30T20:53:40Z","updated_at":"2026-05-30T20:53:40Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Summary\n\nThe `pp-cli` reference verifier accepts a valid Ed25519 signature even when the remotely resolved signing-key record is explicitly marked `status: \"revoked\"`.\n\nThis is distinct from receipt-level `status` validation: `src/keyResolver.ts` selects a remote key by `keyId` and returns its public key material without inspecting key lifecycle metadata. A receipt signed with a compromised former signing key can therefore still verify locally after that key has been revoked, as long as a key-discovery response returns the historical key record.\n\nThe public signing documentation states that `GET /api/v1/keys/:keyId` may return `active`, `rotated`, or `revoked`, and that a revoked key must fail verification immediately.\n\n## Affected code\n\nRepository: `permission-protocol/pp-cli`\nCurrent `main`: `0d282b947a4a3d8080182ae954b3c7d8c84059bd`\n\n`src/keyResolver.ts` currently models only key id and key material:\n\n```ts\ntype RemoteKeyRecord = {\n  keyId?: string;\n  id?: string;\n  publicKey?: string;\n  key?: string;\n};\n```\n\n`pickKeyFromPayload()` matches the identifier and returns `publicKey` / `key`. It does not inspect `status`. `verifyReceipt()` subsequently verifies the signature and only rejects receipt-level revocation, not key-level revocation.\n\n## Local reproduction\n\nThis uses the repository fixture key and a local `data:` key-discovery response, so it does not call production infrastructure.\n\n```bash\nnpm ci\nnpm run build\n\nKEY=\"$(tr -d '\\r\\n' < tests/fixtures/public-key.base64)\"\nPAYLOAD=\"$(node -e 'console.log(JSON.stringify({keyId:\"pp-test-2026-q2\",algorithm:\"ed25519\",publicKey:process.argv[1],status:\"revoked\",createdAt:\"2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z\"}))' \"$KEY\")\"\nURL=\"data:application/json,$(node -e 'console.log(encodeURIComponent(process.argv[1]))' \"$PAYLOAD\")\"\n\nnode dist/cli.js verify tests/fixtures/valid.json --key-url \"$URL\" --json\necho $?\n```\n\nObserved result:\n\n```text\n\"verified\": true\nexit code: 0\n```\n\nThe fixture receipt is mathematically signed by the fixture private key. The bypass is that the verifier still treats that signature as authorization-valid after remote key metadata explicitly revokes the signing key.\n\n## Impact\n\nKey rotation is the containment mechanism for a compromised Ed25519 signing key. Ignoring `status: \"revoked\"` allows receipts signed by a revoked private key to remain locally acceptable to CLI consumers that rely on exit code `0` as their authorization decision.\n\n`rotated` keys should remain usable for historical verification according to the documentation; `revoked` keys must fail closed.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\n- Parse lifecycle metadata for the selected remote key record.\n- Reject `status: \"revoked\"` before returning usable key material.\n- Prefer failing closed for unknown explicit remote key statuses.\n- Add a regression test where the existing valid fixture is verified against a matching remote key record marked `revoked` and must fail key resolution.\n\n## Bounty note\n\nSubmitted for `permission-protocol/deploy-gate#36`: this is a flaw in the Ed25519 key-revocation verification flow, not a raw signature forgery. Payout details can be provided privately after validation.\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/permission-protocol/deploy-gate/issues/50/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/permission-protocol/deploy-gate/issues/50/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/2014","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/2014/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/2014/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/2014/events","html_url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/2014","id":4554347152,"node_id":"I_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABD3XSkA","number":2014,"title":"API test script should discover test files instead of loading test directory","user":{"login":"Ceyvion","id":58273467,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4MjczNDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/58273467?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ceyvion","html_url":"https://github.com/Ceyvion","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ceyvion/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ceyvion/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ceyvion/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ceyvion/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ceyvion/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ceyvion/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ceyvion/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ceyvion/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ceyvion/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-30T12:15:04Z","updated_at":"2026-05-30T12:15:04Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Bug\n\nThe API workspace test script currently runs `node --test src/tests`:\n\n```json\n\"test\": \"node --test src/tests\"\n```\n\nOn the current Node runtime, that treats `src/tests` as an entry module path and fails before discovering the existing `src/tests/health.test.js` file:\n\n```text\nError: Cannot find module .../apps/api/src/tests\ncode: MODULE_NOT_FOUND\n```\n\n## Impact\n\n- `npm test -w apps/api` fails even though the API test file itself passes.\n- Contributors cannot use the documented/package test command to validate API-only changes.\n- The failing workspace script hides real test results behind a test-discovery error.\n\n## Expected behavior\n\n`npm test -w apps/api` should use Node test discovery and run the API test files successfully.\n\n## Proposed fix\n\n- Change the API test script to `node --test`.\n- Verify `npm test -w apps/api` passes from the monorepo root.\n- Keep the change scoped to the API package script.\n\nThis issue is limited only to the creator of this issue. This means that only the issue author can attempt to solve this issue. If you would like to work on it, please create another issue with the same contents and refer to issue #743 for more information.\n\nParent bounty: #743.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/2014/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/2014/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/etherisc/depeg-ui/issues/215","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/etherisc/depeg-ui","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/etherisc/depeg-ui/issues/215/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/etherisc/depeg-ui/issues/215/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/etherisc/depeg-ui/issues/215/events","html_url":"https://github.com/etherisc/depeg-ui/issues/215","id":1560670159,"node_id":"I_kwDOIX5usM5dBe_P","number":215,"title":"[MetaMask Mobile] \"Switch to network Polygon mumbai\" button does nothing","user":{"login":"gebunu","id":64384431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0Mzg0NDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64384431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gebunu","html_url":"https://github.com/gebunu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gebunu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gebunu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gebunu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gebunu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gebunu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gebunu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gebunu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gebunu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gebunu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":4762440956,"node_id":"LA_kwDOIX5usM8AAAABG90U_A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/etherisc/depeg-ui/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working"},{"id":4859404339,"node_id":"LA_kwDOIX5usM8AAAABIaSgMw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/etherisc/depeg-ui/labels/ui","name":"ui","color":"0052cc","default":false,"description":""},{"id":5069818131,"node_id":"LA_kwDOIX5usM8AAAABLi9JEw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/etherisc/depeg-ui/labels/informational","name":"informational","color":"5319E7","default":false,"description":""},{"id":5074994355,"node_id":"LA_kwDOIX5usM8AAAABLn5Esw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/etherisc/depeg-ui/labels/bug%20bounty","name":"bug bounty","color":"6ACAA5","default":false,"description":""},{"id":5074996157,"node_id":"LA_kwDOIX5usM8AAAABLn5LvQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/etherisc/depeg-ui/labels/bug%20bounty%20accepted","name":"bug bounty accepted","color":"8F69FD","default":false,"description":""}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2023-01-28T03:27:52Z","updated_at":"2026-05-27T14:38:03Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### What happened?\n\nUpon clicking the button, nothing happens. Opening straight from the MetaMask App\n\n### What operating system are you seeing the problem on?\n\nAndroid\n\n### What browsers are you seeing the problem on?\n\nOther (please mention in the description)\n\n### What wallet extension are you using?\n\nMetamask\n\n### Rules\n\n- [X] I agree to follow this project's rules","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/etherisc/depeg-ui/issues/215/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/etherisc/depeg-ui/issues/215/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/lucid-agents/issues/181","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/lucid-agents","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/lucid-agents/issues/181/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/lucid-agents/issues/181/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/lucid-agents/issues/181/events","html_url":"https://github.com/daydreamsai/lucid-agents/issues/181","id":3994314672,"node_id":"I_kwDOQPXP0s7uFGew","number":181,"title":"[Data API] Supplier Reliability Signal Marketplace API (TDD PRD)","user":{"login":"ponderingdemocritus","id":90423308,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNDIzMzA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90423308?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus","html_url":"https://github.com/ponderingdemocritus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10296243754,"node_id":"LA_kwDOQPXP0s8AAAACZbQ2Kg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/lucid-agents/labels/BOUNTY","name":"BOUNTY","color":"1D76DB","default":false,"description":"Taskmarket bounty linked issue"},{"id":10296243804,"node_id":"LA_kwDOQPXP0s8AAAACZbQ2XA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/lucid-agents/labels/AMOUNT:%20$3","name":"AMOUNT: $3","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"Bounty amount is $3"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":7,"created_at":"2026-02-26T09:19:11Z","updated_at":"2026-05-27T03:28:57Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## TDD PRD\n\n### Context\nBuild a paid supplier-intelligence API selling lead-time drift, fill-rate risk, and disruption probability.\n\n### Problem\nProcurement agents cannot consistently compare supplier reliability across regions and product categories.\n\n### Buyer User Story (Agent-to-Agent)\nAs a sourcing agent, I need normalized reliability signals and confidence bands to choose resilient suppliers under constraints.\n\n### Product Scope\n- Sell data through paid HTTP endpoints (x402) for machine consumers.\n- Expose deterministic JSON contracts with strict Zod validation.\n- Provide freshness metadata and confidence annotations in every response.\n- Support programmatic agent consumers via stable API versioning.\n\n### API Contract (v1)\n- Endpoints: GET /v1/suppliers/score, GET /v1/suppliers/lead-time-forecast, GET /v1/suppliers/disruption-alerts\n- Inputs: supplierId, category, region, horizonDays, riskTolerance\n- Outputs: supplier_score, lead_time_p50_p95, disruption_probability, alert_reasons, freshness_ms\n\n### Architecture Requirements (Lucid Packages)\n- Runtime: @lucid-agents/core\n- Transport + SSE: @lucid-agents/http\n- Paywall + pricing: @lucid-agents/payments\n- Receivables wallet: @lucid-agents/wallet\n- Trust & attestations: @lucid-agents/identity\n- Upstream agent federation: @lucid-agents/a2a\n- Revenue sharing and composable payments: @lucid-agents/ap2\n\n### TDD Plan (Required Sequence)\n1. Write failing contract tests for all request/response schemas and error envelopes.\n2. Write failing business-logic tests for core data transforms and ranking/scoring behavior.\n3. Write failing integration tests for paid-route behavior (x402 required on monetized endpoints).\n4. Write failing freshness/quality tests (staleness thresholds, confidence propagation).\n5. Implement minimum code to pass tests incrementally.\n6. Refactor with tests green, preserving API behavior and performance budgets.\n\n### Test Coverage Requirements\n- Focus: forecast backtests, anomaly detection tests, ranking consistency, paid endpoint guards, SLA freshness assertions\n- Unit: schema parsing, pure transforms, scoring/ranking invariants.\n- Integration: endpoint handlers + payment middleware + A2A upstream adapters.\n- Contract: stable JSON shape, explicit error codes, backwards-compatible field semantics.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- All monetized endpoints require payment and return valid data after successful payment.\n- All responses include freshness and confidence fields where relevant.\n- P95 response time for cached path <= 500ms under test workload.\n- Test suite passes in CI with no skipped critical tests.\n- README includes endpoint examples for agent consumers.\n\n### Deliverables\n- Source implementation with typed contracts.\n- Test suite (unit + integration + contract).\n- API docs/examples for machine consumers.\n- Configuration docs for pricing and receivable wallet.\n\n### Definition of Done\n- PR opened referencing this issue.\n- CI green with test evidence attached.\n- Reviewer confirms TDD order from commit history and test evolution.\n\n### TaskMarket Cross-Reference\n- TaskMarket Task ID: 0xeae805c5e9439f832fe1a74ec1778252913174e11b833a1f3d1a5b7296adb36b\n- TaskMarket API URL: https://api-market.daydreams.systems/api/tasks/0xeae805c5e9439f832fe1a74ec1778252913174e11b833a1f3d1a5b7296adb36b\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/lucid-agents/issues/181/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/lucid-agents/issues/181/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/lucid-agents/issues/184","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/lucid-agents","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/lucid-agents/issues/184/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/lucid-agents/issues/184/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/lucid-agents/issues/184/events","html_url":"https://github.com/daydreamsai/lucid-agents/issues/184","id":3994316858,"node_id":"I_kwDOQPXP0s7uFHA6","number":184,"title":"[Data API] Data Freshness & Provenance Verification API (TDD PRD)","user":{"login":"ponderingdemocritus","id":90423308,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNDIzMzA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90423308?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus","html_url":"https://github.com/ponderingdemocritus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ponderingdemocritus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10296243754,"node_id":"LA_kwDOQPXP0s8AAAACZbQ2Kg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/lucid-agents/labels/BOUNTY","name":"BOUNTY","color":"1D76DB","default":false,"description":"Taskmarket bounty linked issue"},{"id":10296243804,"node_id":"LA_kwDOQPXP0s8AAAACZbQ2XA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/lucid-agents/labels/AMOUNT:%20$3","name":"AMOUNT: $3","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"Bounty amount is $3"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":8,"created_at":"2026-02-26T09:19:37Z","updated_at":"2026-05-27T03:28:00Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## TDD PRD\n\n### Context\nBuild a paid verification API selling dataset freshness SLAs, lineage graphs, and tamper-check attestations.\n\n### Problem\nDecision agents consume stale or unverifiable upstream data and cannot quantify trust quickly.\n\n### Buyer User Story (Agent-to-Agent)\nAs a strategy agent, I need freshness and provenance checks before using external datasets in automated decisions.\n\n### Product Scope\n- Sell data through paid HTTP endpoints (x402) for machine consumers.\n- Expose deterministic JSON contracts with strict Zod validation.\n- Provide freshness metadata and confidence annotations in every response.\n- Support programmatic agent consumers via stable API versioning.\n\n### API Contract (v1)\n- Endpoints: GET /v1/provenance/lineage, GET /v1/provenance/freshness, POST /v1/provenance/verify-hash\n- Inputs: datasetId, sourceId, expectedHash, maxStalenessMs\n- Outputs: lineage_graph, staleness_ms, sla_status, verification_status, attestation_refs\n\n### Architecture Requirements (Lucid Packages)\n- Runtime: @lucid-agents/core\n- Transport + SSE: @lucid-agents/http\n- Paywall + pricing: @lucid-agents/payments\n- Receivables wallet: @lucid-agents/wallet\n- Trust & attestations: @lucid-agents/identity\n- Upstream agent federation: @lucid-agents/a2a\n- Revenue sharing and composable payments: @lucid-agents/ap2\n\n### TDD Plan (Required Sequence)\n1. Write failing contract tests for all request/response schemas and error envelopes.\n2. Write failing business-logic tests for core data transforms and ranking/scoring behavior.\n3. Write failing integration tests for paid-route behavior (x402 required on monetized endpoints).\n4. Write failing freshness/quality tests (staleness thresholds, confidence propagation).\n5. Implement minimum code to pass tests incrementally.\n6. Refactor with tests green, preserving API behavior and performance budgets.\n\n### Test Coverage Requirements\n- Focus: hash verification tests, lineage graph integrity tests, SLA threshold behavior, paywall tests, schema compatibility tests\n- Unit: schema parsing, pure transforms, scoring/ranking invariants.\n- Integration: endpoint handlers + payment middleware + A2A upstream adapters.\n- Contract: stable JSON shape, explicit error codes, backwards-compatible field semantics.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- All monetized endpoints require payment and return valid data after successful payment.\n- All responses include freshness and confidence fields where relevant.\n- P95 response time for cached path <= 500ms under test workload.\n- Test suite passes in CI with no skipped critical tests.\n- README includes endpoint examples for agent consumers.\n\n### Deliverables\n- Source implementation with typed contracts.\n- Test suite (unit + integration + contract).\n- API docs/examples for machine consumers.\n- Configuration docs for pricing and receivable wallet.\n\n### Definition of Done\n- PR opened referencing this issue.\n- CI green with test evidence attached.\n- Reviewer confirms TDD order from commit history and test evolution.\n\n### TaskMarket Cross-Reference\n- TaskMarket Task ID: 0x99f21ee2bd483a83780ad98a452bfae6ac5531f39d4dfb821a03de1dbd31e5a4\n- TaskMarket API URL: https://api-market.daydreams.systems/api/tasks/0x99f21ee2bd483a83780ad98a452bfae6ac5531f39d4dfb821a03de1dbd31e5a4\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/lucid-agents/issues/184/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/daydreamsai/lucid-agents/issues/184/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0}],"search_type":"lexical"}